{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794565099997,"sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d46a4e2b001w1j4B6cSsFIRu3","sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","messageID":"msg_1d46a36f0001uHMu5b0qbKGqrh","type":"tool","id":"call_55c6f1f43acb44f88c76d000","tool":"skill","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"id":"sk-code"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"sk-code\">\n# Skill: sk-code\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet, guard, adapter, stderr, detector -->\n\n# Code Family Hub (sk-code)\n\nOne skill has two axes, one shared surface-detection router and one advisor identity.\nThe **workflow axis** has two code modes that act: sk-code-quality and sk-code-review.\nThe **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\nEach packet carries the shared **implement → debug → verify** workflow doctrine (`shared/references/workflow-*.md`, symlinked in) plus its own domain knowledge.\nThis hub holds NO per-mode logic. It routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each mode or surface keeps its own contract in its packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`.\n`description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value. Each hub-root JSON routing file therefore states the same release.\n`ROUTER.md` and `README.md` keep their own document versions, as the frontmatter-versioning standard gives every doc but `SKILL.md`.\nThe authority stops at the hub root. Each `modes[]` packet carries its own version and release cadence.\nA packet version is independent of this one by design, so a gap between them is not drift.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for code-family workflows. Invoke it as `sk-code` with an optional mode hint such as `quality: <request>`. The hub classifies the request, resolves a mode key, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n**Workflow axis** (modes that act, one of them chosen as primary):\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet |\n|------|------------|--------|\n| **sk-code-quality** | Quality gate, P0/P1/P2 author checks, comment hygiene and surface checklists. | `sk-code/sk-code-quality/` |\n| **sk-code-review** | Findings-first review, security and correctness baseline, checklists, output contract and PR-state gates. | `sk-code/sk-code-review/` |\n\n**Surface axis** (read-only, advisor-invisible evidence. When a workflow mode scores, the hub bundles the surface after that primary mode. When no workflow mode scores, the hub routes the surface alone for a lookup, implement, debug or verify task, and the acting agent hands the author gates to `sk-code-quality` before it claims completion):\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, visual values, visual hierarchy and review, motion and interaction, the `tokens.css` starter tokens and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, with visual values, visual hierarchy and review, and motion and interaction guidance, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\nAny other sk-code doc that counts surfaces points to this sentence.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Documentation-only changes with no code-work contract - use `sk-doc`.\n- Git workflow, branch, commit, PR, merge, or release work - use `sk-git`.\n- Pure browser inspection or external MCP transport work - use the relevant MCP skill.\n- For a measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source), use `sk-design-md-generator` first.\n- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n- Backend support primitives in `shared/` - they are consumed by the modes, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) uses `hub-router.json` as the authored mode vocabulary. `mode-registry.json` carries the packet contracts, whose aliases are checked against that vocabulary.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) uses the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) as the authored leaf-set router.\nBoth files point back here instead of restating the split.\n\nThe advisor routes every code query to the single identity `sk-code`. Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt \"<task>\"` and follow the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default. The legacy fallback, the kill-switch and the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` live in the compiled-routing section of [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n\nA bare implement, debug or verify request with no workflow mode becomes a pure surface bundle, and an unclear code intent asks for disambiguation. Neither path forces a stale default.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode or surface key a request resolves to.\n- **`packetKind`**: the axis a packet sits on, `workflow` for a mode that acts and `surface` for read-only evidence bundled alongside a mode.\n- **`backendKind`**: which backend runs the packet, `surface-router` or `review-cache` for a workflow mode and `evidence-base` for a surface.\n- **`surfaceBundle`**: the `routerPolicy.outcomes` entry where one workflow mode leads and zero or more surfaces follow as evidence.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each mode's discriminator, `surfaceDetection` markers and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's `routerSignals`, `vocabularyClasses` and the surface-bundling policy.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, plus the `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` list and the always-loaded `DEFAULT_RESOURCE` preamble.\n- **shared control**: a hub-level resource declared in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, which resolves on disk and never projects as a leaf.\n- **leaf**: a typed `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **surface detection**: the shared detection order over the declared surfaces, which tries each specific surface first, then the `SKILLED` fallback, then `UNKNOWN`.\n- **`--surface-hint`**: the front-door flag that carries the detected surface into the compiled route, so a hinted surface leads a keyword tie.\n- **`UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`**: the load level the router returns, with a disambiguation checklist, when no mode resolves.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-code/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-mode code logic)\n  README.md              # human-facing front page for the hub\n  ROUTER.md              # active stage-two surface router and shared-control declaration\n  mode-registry.json     # the two-axis discriminator + advisorRouting contract\n  hub-router.json        # lexical routing signals + surfaceBundle policy for hub-local choice\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  leaf-manifest.json     # typed (workflowMode, leaf) pairs the router guards validate\n  changelog/             # hub release notes, one v<version>.md per hub release\n  feature-catalog/       # current-state inventory of the hub's routing capabilities\n  manual-testing-playbook/  # routing and disambiguation scenarios for the hub\n  benchmark/             # historical routing benchmark inputs and reports\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only; references/web-visual-values.md, web-visual-hierarchy.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md plus assets/tokens.css)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n\nEach mode or surface packet is self-contained and carries no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`. Only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one code skill identity. The implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine is a single shared source under `shared/references/`, and each surface symlinks it in rather than duplicating it.\n\n### Backend\nThe `surface-router` backend is the shared surface-detection router under `shared/`.\nIt centralizes the detection order over the declared surfaces, the SKILLED fallback and UNKNOWN.\nIt carries the shared implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine consumed by each surface.\nThe `review-cache` backend supports the sk-code-review mode's non-mutating review output cache.\nThe `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\nThe packet mutates nothing and never carries process. The acting agent applies the doctrine it bundles.\nShared backend material provides surface identity, the workflow doctrine and cross-mode helpers.\nIt must never gain per-mode workflow contracts.\n\nThe **implement → debug → verify** phases are not standalone modes.\nTheir surface-agnostic doctrine lives once in `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `workflow-debug.md` and `workflow-verify.md`.\nThose files are symlinked into each surface, so the active surface carries the full workflow.\nA request to implement, debug or verify code causes the router to detect its surface and load that surface's bundled doctrine.\nThe acting agent applies that doctrine.\n\n### Maintenance\n\nAfter adding or removing a surface, run `/doctor:sk-code setup`. It checks the hub and names the repair for each failing check.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a mode through `mode-registry.json`, and never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep mode contracts in the mode packets, so the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one skill identity.\n- **ALWAYS** give every mode an `advisorRouting` block with `routingClass: \"metadata\"` and the correct `packetSkillName`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine as one shared source under `shared/references/`, symlinked into each surface, and never fork per-surface copies.\n- **ALWAYS** keep `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned with its intent keys and packet leaves aligned with `leaf-manifest.json`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep hub-shared map inputs explicit in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, because they are control resources and never typed leaves.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a mode packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-mode quality, review, or surface workflow logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** hardcode a router mapping outside `mode-registry.json`.\n- **NEVER** reintroduce implement, debug, or verify as standalone mode packets, because they are surface-owned doctrine.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new code mode is needed - extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet. Do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- Surface identity and workflow ownership conflict in a way the shared router cannot classify.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Workflow mode packets: `sk-code-quality/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md`.\n- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n- Shared workflow doctrine: `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `shared/references/workflow-debug.md`, `shared/references/workflow-verify.md` (symlinked into each surface).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (two-axis: `packetKind` discriminates workflow vs surface).\n- Hub router signals + surface bundling: `hub-router.json`.\n- Surface router and shared controls: `ROUTER.md`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n- Sibling example: `.skilled/skills/sk-prompt/`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/findings-and-recommendations.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.json</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","title":"skill","metadata":{"metadata":{"name":"sk-code","directory":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code","truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<skill_content name=\"sk-code\">\n# Skill: sk-code\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet, guard, adapter, stderr, detector -->\n\n# Code Family Hub (sk-code)\n\nOne skill has two axes, one shared surface-detection router and one advisor identity.\nThe **workflow axis** has two code modes that act: sk-code-quality and sk-code-review.\nThe **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\nEach packet carries the shared **implement → debug → verify** workflow doctrine (`shared/references/workflow-*.md`, symlinked in) plus its own domain knowledge.\nThis hub holds NO per-mode logic. It routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each mode or surface keeps its own contract in its packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`.\n`description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value. Each hub-root JSON routing file therefore states the same release.\n`ROUTER.md` and `README.md` keep their own document versions, as the frontmatter-versioning standard gives every doc but `SKILL.md`.\nThe authority stops at the hub root. Each `modes[]` packet carries its own version and release cadence.\nA packet version is independent of this one by design, so a gap between them is not drift.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for code-family workflows. Invoke it as `sk-code` with an optional mode hint such as `quality: <request>`. The hub classifies the request, resolves a mode key, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n**Workflow axis** (modes that act, one of them chosen as primary):\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet |\n|------|------------|--------|\n| **sk-code-quality** | Quality gate, P0/P1/P2 author checks, comment hygiene and surface checklists. | `sk-code/sk-code-quality/` |\n| **sk-code-review** | Findings-first review, security and correctness baseline, checklists, output contract and PR-state gates. | `sk-code/sk-code-review/` |\n\n**Surface axis** (read-only, advisor-invisible evidence. When a workflow mode scores, the hub bundles the surface after that primary mode. When no workflow mode scores, the hub routes the surface alone for a lookup, implement, debug or verify task, and the acting agent hands the author gates to `sk-code-quality` before it claims completion):\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, visual values, visual hierarchy and review, motion and interaction, the `tokens.css` starter tokens and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, with visual values, visual hierarchy and review, and motion and interaction guidance, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\nAny other sk-code doc that counts surfaces points to this sentence.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Documentation-only changes with no code-work contract - use `sk-doc`.\n- Git workflow, branch, commit, PR, merge, or release work - use `sk-git`.\n- Pure browser inspection or external MCP transport work - use the relevant MCP skill.\n- For a measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source), use `sk-design-md-generator` first.\n- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n- Backend support primitives in `shared/` - they are consumed by the modes, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) uses `hub-router.json` as the authored mode vocabulary. `mode-registry.json` carries the packet contracts, whose aliases are checked against that vocabulary.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) uses the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) as the authored leaf-set router.\nBoth files point back here instead of restating the split.\n\nThe advisor routes every code query to the single identity `sk-code`. Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt \"<task>\"` and follow the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default. The legacy fallback, the kill-switch and the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` live in the compiled-routing section of [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n\nA bare implement, debug or verify request with no workflow mode becomes a pure surface bundle, and an unclear code intent asks for disambiguation. Neither path forces a stale default.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode or surface key a request resolves to.\n- **`packetKind`**: the axis a packet sits on, `workflow` for a mode that acts and `surface` for read-only evidence bundled alongside a mode.\n- **`backendKind`**: which backend runs the packet, `surface-router` or `review-cache` for a workflow mode and `evidence-base` for a surface.\n- **`surfaceBundle`**: the `routerPolicy.outcomes` entry where one workflow mode leads and zero or more surfaces follow as evidence.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each mode's discriminator, `surfaceDetection` markers and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's `routerSignals`, `vocabularyClasses` and the surface-bundling policy.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, plus the `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` list and the always-loaded `DEFAULT_RESOURCE` preamble.\n- **shared control**: a hub-level resource declared in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, which resolves on disk and never projects as a leaf.\n- **leaf**: a typed `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **surface detection**: the shared detection order over the declared surfaces, which tries each specific surface first, then the `SKILLED` fallback, then `UNKNOWN`.\n- **`--surface-hint`**: the front-door flag that carries the detected surface into the compiled route, so a hinted surface leads a keyword tie.\n- **`UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`**: the load level the router returns, with a disambiguation checklist, when no mode resolves.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-code/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-mode code logic)\n  README.md              # human-facing front page for the hub\n  ROUTER.md              # active stage-two surface router and shared-control declaration\n  mode-registry.json     # the two-axis discriminator + advisorRouting contract\n  hub-router.json        # lexical routing signals + surfaceBundle policy for hub-local choice\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  leaf-manifest.json     # typed (workflowMode, leaf) pairs the router guards validate\n  changelog/             # hub release notes, one v<version>.md per hub release\n  feature-catalog/       # current-state inventory of the hub's routing capabilities\n  manual-testing-playbook/  # routing and disambiguation scenarios for the hub\n  benchmark/             # historical routing benchmark inputs and reports\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only; references/web-visual-values.md, web-visual-hierarchy.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md plus assets/tokens.css)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n\nEach mode or surface packet is self-contained and carries no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`. Only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one code skill identity. The implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine is a single shared source under `shared/references/`, and each surface symlinks it in rather than duplicating it.\n\n### Backend\nThe `surface-router` backend is the shared surface-detection router under `shared/`.\nIt centralizes the detection order over the declared surfaces, the SKILLED fallback and UNKNOWN.\nIt carries the shared implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine consumed by each surface.\nThe `review-cache` backend supports the sk-code-review mode's non-mutating review output cache.\nThe `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\nThe packet mutates nothing and never carries process. The acting agent applies the doctrine it bundles.\nShared backend material provides surface identity, the workflow doctrine and cross-mode helpers.\nIt must never gain per-mode workflow contracts.\n\nThe **implement → debug → verify** phases are not standalone modes.\nTheir surface-agnostic doctrine lives once in `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `workflow-debug.md` and `workflow-verify.md`.\nThose files are symlinked into each surface, so the active surface carries the full workflow.\nA request to implement, debug or verify code causes the router to detect its surface and load that surface's bundled doctrine.\nThe acting agent applies that doctrine.\n\n### Maintenance\n\nAfter adding or removing a surface, run `/doctor:sk-code setup`. It checks the hub and names the repair for each failing check.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a mode through `mode-registry.json`, and never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep mode contracts in the mode packets, so the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one skill identity.\n- **ALWAYS** give every mode an `advisorRouting` block with `routingClass: \"metadata\"` and the correct `packetSkillName`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine as one shared source under `shared/references/`, symlinked into each surface, and never fork per-surface copies.\n- **ALWAYS** keep `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned with its intent keys and packet leaves aligned with `leaf-manifest.json`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep hub-shared map inputs explicit in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, because they are control resources and never typed leaves.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a mode packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-mode quality, review, or surface workflow logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** hardcode a router mapping outside `mode-registry.json`.\n- **NEVER** reintroduce implement, debug, or verify as standalone mode packets, because they are surface-owned doctrine.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new code mode is needed - extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet. Do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- Surface identity and workflow ownership conflict in a way the shared router cannot classify.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Workflow mode packets: `sk-code-quality/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md`.\n- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n- Shared workflow doctrine: `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `shared/references/workflow-debug.md`, `shared/references/workflow-verify.md` (symlinked into each surface).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (two-axis: `packetKind` discriminates workflow vs surface).\n- Hub router signals + surface bundling: `hub-router.json`.\n- Surface router and shared controls: `ROUTER.md`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n- Sibling example: `.skilled/skills/sk-prompt/`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/findings-and-recommendations.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.json</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"id\":\"sk-code\"}"},"time":{"start":1794565099051,"end":1794565099997}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794565100002,"sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d46a4ead001mbtjxSsaI8obb7","sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","messageID":"msg_1d46a36f0001uHMu5b0qbKGqrh","type":"tool","id":"call_ca4e58269ecb47b8ade6327e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts, lines 1-563\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: advisor_status Handler\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\n10: import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n11: import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n12: \n13: import { computeAdvisorSourceSignature } from '../lib/freshness.js';\n14: import { readSkillGraphGeneration } from '../lib/freshness/generation.js';\n15: import { checkSqliteIntegrity } from '../lib/freshness/sqlite-integrity.js';\n16: import { createPrivateSkillLinkCheck } from '../lib/private-skill-target.js';\n17: import {\n18:   computeSkillMetadataContentHash,\n19:   isGenuineCorruptionReason,\n20:   readCommandEmbeddingSources,\n21:   resolveSkillGraphDbDir,\n22:   DB_FILENAME,\n23: } from '../lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js';\n24: import { createTrustState } from '../lib/freshness/trust-state.js';\n25: import { getAdapter, getManifest } from '../lib/embedders/registry.js';\n26: import { probeOllamaModel, resolveOllamaBaseUrl } from '../lib/embedders/adapters/ollama.js';\n27: import { commandVecTableNameForDim } from '../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n28: import { readEmbeddingsHealth } from '../lib/embedders/embeddings-health.js';\n29: import { getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth } from '../lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js';\n30: import { readAdvisorEmbeddingStaleness } from '../lib/scorer/projection.js';\n31: import { DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS } from '../lib/scorer/weights-config.js';\n32: import { readAdvisorHookHealthSection } from '../lib/metrics.js';\n33: import { errorMessage } from '../lib/utils/error-format.js';\n34: import { redactDiagnosticText } from './skill-graph/response-envelope.js';\n35: import {\n36:   AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n37:   AdvisorStatusOutputSchema,\n38: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n39: \n40: import type {\n41:   AdvisorFreshness,\n42:   AdvisorStatusInput,\n43:   AdvisorStatusOutput,\n44: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n45: \n46: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n47: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS AND CONSTANTS\n48: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: \n50: type HandlerResponse = { content: Array<{ type: string; text: string }> };\n51: type IndexStaleness = NonNullable<AdvisorStatusOutput['indexStaleness']>;\n52: \n53: const SKILL_ROOT = join('.skilled', 'skills');\n54: const DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES = 5_000;\n55: type SemanticLaneHealth = NonNullable<AdvisorStatusOutput['semanticLaneHealth']>;\n56: \n57: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: // 3. HELPERS\n59: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n60: \n61: function isFreshness(value: string): value is AdvisorFreshness {\n62:   return value === 'live' || value === 'stale' || value === 'absent' || value === 'unavailable';\n63: }\n64: \n65: function parseDaemonPid(): number | undefined {\n66:   const raw = process.env.SPECKIT_SKILL_GRAPH_DAEMON_PID;\n67:   if (!raw) return undefined;\n68:   const parsed = Number(raw);\n69:   return Number.isSafeInteger(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : undefined;\n70: }\n71: \n72: function hasRunningDaemon(pid: number | undefined): boolean {\n73:   if (!pid) {\n74:     return false;\n75:   }\n76:   try {\n77:     process.kill(pid, 0);\n78:     return true;\n79:   } catch {\n80:     return false;\n81:   }\n82: }\n83: \n84: function fileMtimeMs(path: string): number {\n85:   if (!existsSync(path)) return 0;\n86:   const stat = statSync(path);\n87:   return stat.mtimeMs;\n88: }\n89: \n90: function resolveSkillGraphDbPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n91:   // Resolve through the writer's own resolver so the integrity probe always\n92:   // targets the exact file the daemon writes. An env override wins for both;\n93:   // otherwise the workspace root stands in for the writer's cwd, which match\n94:   // in the normal single-root deployment.\n95:   return join(resolveSkillGraphDbDir(workspaceRoot), DB_FILENAME);\n96: }\n97: \n98: // Per-(dbPath, generation, mtime) integrity verdict cache. A full quick_check\n99: // scans the artifact, which is too costly to run on the recommend hot path;\n100: // caching it lets recommend opt into corruption detection while paying the\n101: // scan at most once per generation. The only events that can change on-disk\n102: // integrity — a generation bump or an mtime change — invalidate the entry.\n103: const integrityVerdictCache = new Map<string, { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string }>();\n104: \n105: function checkSqliteIntegrityCached(\n106:   dbPath: string,\n107:   generation: number,\n108:   mtimeMs: number,\n109: ): { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string } {\n110:   const key = `${dbPath}::${generation}::${mtimeMs}`;\n111:   const cached = integrityVerdictCache.get(key);\n112:   if (cached) {\n113:     return cached;\n114:   }\n115:   const result = checkSqliteIntegrity(dbPath);\n116:   // Only the newest (path, generation, mtime) verdict is ever consulted, so a\n117:   // single-entry cache is sufficient and self-bounding.\n118:   integrityVerdictCache.clear();\n119:   integrityVerdictCache.set(key, result);\n120:   return result;\n121: }\n122: \n123: function tableExists(database: Database.Database, tableName: string): boolean {\n124:   const row = database.prepare(`\n125:     SELECT 1 AS present\n126:     FROM sqlite_master\n127:     WHERE type = 'table' AND name = ?\n128:     LIMIT 1\n129:   `).get(tableName) as { present: number } | undefined;\n130:   return Boolean(row);\n131: }\n132: \n133: function metadataValue(database: Database.Database, key: string): string | null {\n134:   if (!tableExists(database, 'vec_metadata')) return null;\n135:   const row = database.prepare('SELECT value FROM vec_metadata WHERE key = ?').get(key) as { value: string } | undefined;\n136:   return row?.value ?? null;\n137: }\n138: \n139: function countRows(database: Database.Database, sql: string): number {\n140:   const row = database.prepare(sql).get() as { c: number } | undefined;\n141:   return row?.c ?? 0;\n142: }\n143: \n144: function maxUpdatedAt(database: Database.Database, tableName: string): string | null {\n145:   const row = database.prepare(`SELECT MAX(updated_at) AS updatedAt FROM ${tableName}`).get() as { updatedAt: string | null } | undefined;\n146:   return row?.updatedAt ?? null;\n147: }\n148: \n149: function baseSemanticLaneHealth(disabledReason: string | null): SemanticLaneHealth {\n150:   return {\n151:     activeEmbedder: null,\n152:     vectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: 0, ratio: 0 },\n153:     dimMismatch: false,\n154:     lastRefresh: null,\n155:     disabledReason,\n156:     laneEnabled: false,\n157:     checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n158:   };\n159: }\n160: \n161: function readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath: string): SemanticLaneHealth {\n162:   const runtime = getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth();\n163:   // The command projection's size does not depend on the database, so the\n164:   // denominator is known even when the artifact is missing or unreadable.\n165:   const commandTotal = readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0;\n166:   if (!existsSync(dbPath)) {\n167:     return {\n168:       ...baseSemanticLaneHealth(runtime.disabledReason ?? 'database_absent'),\n169:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: commandTotal },\n170:     };\n171:   }\n172: \n173:   let database: Database.Database | null = null;\n174:   try {\n175:     database = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n176:     const total = tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes')\n177:       ? countRows(database, 'SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM skill_nodes')\n178:       : 0;\n179:     const activeName = metadataValue(database, 'active_embedder_name');\n180:     const activeDimRaw = metadataValue(database, 'active_embedder_dim');\n181:     const activeDim = activeDimRaw ? Number.parseInt(activeDimRaw, 10) : 0;\n182:     const hasActive = Boolean(activeName) && Number.isInteger(activeDim) && activeDim > 0;\n183:     const adapter = activeName ? getAdapter(activeName) : undefined;\n184:     const activeEmbedder = activeName\n185:       ? { name: activeName, dim: Number.isInteger(activeDim) && activeDim > 0 ? activeDim : 0, adapterDim: adapter?.dim ?? null }\n186:       : null;\n187:     const tableName = hasActive ? `vec_${activeDim}` : null;\n188:     const hasVecTable = tableName ? tableExists(database, tableName) : false;\n189:     const embedded = hasVecTable\n190:       ? countRows(database, `SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM ${tableName} WHERE embedding IS NOT NULL`)\n191:       : (tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes') ? countRows(database, 'SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM skill_nodes WHERE embedding IS NOT NULL') : 0);\n192:     const lastRefresh = hasVecTable && tableName ? maxUpdatedAt(database, tableName) : null;\n193:     const commandTable = hasActive ? commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim) : null;\n194:     const commandEmbedded = commandTable && tableExists(database, commandTable)\n195:       ? countRows(database, `SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM ${commandTable}`)\n196:       : 0;\n197:     const dimMismatch = Boolean(activeEmbedder && activeEmbedder.adapterDim !== null && activeEmbedder.dim !== activeEmbedder.adapterDim);\n198:     const staleness = readAdvisorEmbeddingStaleness(database);\n199:     const disabledReason = dimMismatch\n200:       ? 'dim_mismatch'\n201:       : (staleness.stale\n202:           ? 'projection_embedding_stale'\n203:           : (!hasActive\n204:               ? 'active_embedder_unset'\n205:               : (!adapter\n206:                   ? 'adapter_unavailable'\n207:                   : (!hasVecTable\n208:                       ? 'vector_table_missing'\n209:                       : (total > 0 && embedded === 0 ? 'no_skill_vectors' : runtime.disabledReason)))));\n210:     return {\n211:       activeEmbedder,\n212:       vectorCoverage: {\n213:         embedded,\n214:         total,\n215:         ratio: total > 0 ? Math.round((embedded / total) * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000 : 0,\n216:       },\n217:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: commandEmbedded, total: commandTotal },\n218:       dimMismatch,\n219:       lastRefresh,\n220:       disabledReason,\n221:       laneEnabled: Boolean(hasActive && adapter && !dimMismatch && !staleness.stale && hasVecTable && embedded > 0 && !disabledReason),\n222:       checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n223:     };\n224:   } catch {\n225:     return {\n226:       ...baseSemanticLaneHealth(runtime.disabledReason ?? 'health_unavailable'),\n227:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: commandTotal },\n228:     };\n229:   } finally {\n230:     database?.close();\n231:   }\n232: }\n233: \n234: function readIndexStaleness(dbPath: string, workspaceRoot: string): IndexStaleness {\n235:   const unavailable = (reason: string): IndexStaleness => ({\n236:     state: 'unavailable',\n237:     reason,\n238:     trackedSkills: 0,\n239:     freshSourceFiles: 0,\n240:     changedSourceFiles: 0,\n241:     missingSourceFiles: 0,\n242:     staleSkillIds: [],\n243:   });\n244:   if (!existsSync(dbPath)) return unavailable('database_absent');\n245: \n246:   let database: Database.Database | null = null;\n247:   let result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n248:   try {\n249:     database = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n250:     if (!tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes')) {\n251:       result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n252:     } else {\n253:       const columns = database.pragma('table_info(skill_nodes)') as Array<{ name: string }>;\n254:       const hasSourceColumns = columns.some((column) => column.name === 'source_path')\n255:         && columns.some((column) => column.name === 'content_hash');\n256:       if (!hasSourceColumns) {\n257:         result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n258:       } else {\n259:         const rows = database.prepare(`\n260:           SELECT id, source_path, content_hash\n261:           FROM skill_nodes\n262:           ORDER BY id\n263:         `).all() as Array<{\n264:           id: string;\n265:           source_path: string | null;\n266:           content_hash: string | null;\n267:         }>;\n268:         if (rows.length === 0) {\n269:           result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n270:         } else {\n271:           let freshSourceFiles = 0;\n272:           let changedSourceFiles = 0;\n273:           let missingSourceFiles = 0;\n274:           const staleSkillIds: string[] = [];\n275: \n276:           for (const row of rows) {\n277:             if (!row.source_path || row.source_path.trim().length === 0) {\n278:               missingSourceFiles++;\n279:               staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n280:               continue;\n281:             }\n282: \n283:             let content: string;\n284:             try {\n285:               content = readFileSync(resolve(workspaceRoot, row.source_path), 'utf8');\n286:             } catch (error: unknown) {\n287:               if (error instanceof Error && 'code' in error && error.code === 'ENOENT') {\n288:                 missingSourceFiles++;\n289:                 staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n290:                 continue;\n291:               }\n292:               throw error;\n293:             }\n294: \n295:             if (row.content_hash === null\n296:               || computeSkillMetadataContentHash(content) !== row.content_hash) {\n297:               changedSourceFiles++;\n298:               staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n299:               continue;\n300:             }\n301: \n302:             freshSourceFiles++;\n303:           }\n304: \n305:           const stale = changedSourceFiles + missingSourceFiles > 0;\n306:           result = {\n307:             state: stale ? 'stale' : 'fresh',\n308:             reason: stale ? 'source_hash_mismatch' : null,\n309:             trackedSkills: rows.length,\n310:             freshSourceFiles,\n311:             changedSourceFiles,\n312:             missingSourceFiles,\n313:             staleSkillIds: staleSkillIds.slice(0, 25),\n314:           };\n315:         }\n316:       }\n317:     }\n318:   } catch {\n319:     result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n320:   } finally {\n321:     try {\n322:       database?.close();\n323:     } catch {\n324:       result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n325:     }\n326:   }\n327: \n328:   return result;\n329: }\n330: \n331: function scanSkillMetadataFiles(\n332:   skillRoot: string,\n333:   maxFiles = DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES,\n334: ): { count: number; maxMtimeMs: number; truncated: boolean } {\n335:   if (!existsSync(skillRoot)) return { count: 0, maxMtimeMs: 0, truncated: false };\n336:   const isTrustedLink = createPrivateSkillLinkCheck(skillRoot);\n337:   const skillRoots = readdirSync(skillRoot, { withFileTypes: true })\n338:     .filter((entry) => !entry.name.startsWith('.') && (entry.isDirectory()\n339:       || (entry.name.startsWith('local-')\n340:         && entry.isSymbolicLink()\n341:         && isTrustedLink(join(skillRoot, entry.name)))))\n342:     .sort((left, right) => left.name.localeCompare(right.name));\n343:   let count = 0;\n344:   let newest = 0;\n345:   let truncated = false;\n346:   for (const entry of skillRoots) {\n347:     const metadataPath = join(skillRoot, entry.name, 'graph-metadata.json');\n348:     if (!existsSync(metadataPath)) continue;\n349:     const metadataStat = statSync(metadataPath);\n350:     if (!metadataStat.isFile()) continue;\n351:     if (count >= maxFiles) {\n352:       truncated = true;\n353:       break;\n354:     }\n355:     count++;\n356:     newest = Math.max(newest, metadataStat.mtimeMs);\n357:   }\n358:   return { count, maxMtimeMs: newest, truncated };\n359: }\n360: \n361: // The status reader stays synchronous so the recommend path can call it, which\n362: // puts the only network probe here on the async command path. Reading /api/tags\n363: // is the only signal that separates a stopped server or a missing model from a\n364: // healthy lane: the pointer and the vectors survive both, so a lane that\n365: // reports enabled through an outage sends operators to rebuild a fine index\n366: // instead of starting the server.\n367: async function probeSemanticLaneBackend(health: SemanticLaneHealth): Promise<SemanticLaneHealth> {\n368:   const activeName = health.activeEmbedder?.name;\n369:   const manifest = activeName ? getManifest(activeName) : undefined;\n370:   if (!manifest) {\n371:     return health;\n372:   }\n373:   if (manifest.backend !== 'ollama') {\n374:     return {\n375:       ...health,\n376:       backend: { state: 'probe_not_implemented', reason: `no readiness probe for the ${manifest.backend} backend` },\n377:       laneEnabled: false,\n378:     };\n379:   }\n380:   const probe = await probeOllamaModel(\n381:     resolveOllamaBaseUrl(),\n382:     manifest.ollamaName ?? manifest.name,\n383:     500,\n384:   );\n385:   if (probe.available) {\n386:     return { ...health, backend: { state: 'reachable', reason: null } };\n387:   }\n388:   const reason = probe.reason ?? null;\n389:   return {\n390:     ...health,\n391:     backend: {\n392:       state: reason && /not loaded/i.test(reason) ? 'model_missing' : 'unreachable',\n393:       reason,\n394:     },\n395:     laneEnabled: false,\n396:   };\n397: }\n398: \n399: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n400: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n401: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n402: \n403: /** Read advisor freshness state.\n404:  *\n405:  * Diagnostic-only: this function reports stale, absent, or unavailable advisor\n406:  * state and does not rebuild it. Use `advisor_rebuild` to repair stale state.\n407:  */\n408: export function readAdvisorStatus(input: AdvisorStatusInput): AdvisorStatusOutput {\n409:   const args = AdvisorStatusInputSchema.parse(input);\n410:   const workspaceRoot = resolve(args.workspaceRoot);\n411:   const dbPath = resolveSkillGraphDbPath(workspaceRoot);\n412:   const skillRoot = join(workspaceRoot, SKILL_ROOT);\n413:   const errors: string[] = [];\n414: \n415:   try {\n416:     const generation = readSkillGraphGeneration(workspaceRoot);\n417:     const hasSources = existsSync(skillRoot);\n418:     const hasArtifact = existsSync(dbPath);\n419:     // Existence alone lets a corrupt-on-disk artifact report 'live' from the\n420:     // generation counters, which makes advisor_rebuild skip the repair it\n421:     // exists to perform. A read-only quick_check turns genuine corruption\n422:     // into a stale signal so rebuild runs. Transient lock/IO failures are\n423:     // excluded so contention never forces a spurious rebuild.\n424:     const integrity = (hasArtifact && args.checkArtifactIntegrity === true)\n425:       ? checkSqliteIntegrityCached(dbPath, generation.generation, fileMtimeMs(dbPath))\n426:       : null;\n427:     const artifactCorrupt = Boolean(\n428:       integrity && !integrity.ok\n429:         && integrity.reason !== 'SQLITE_ABSENT'\n430:         && isGenuineCorruptionReason(integrity.reason),\n431:     );\n432:     if (artifactCorrupt && integrity && !integrity.ok) {\n433:       errors.push(`advisor_status skill graph integrity check failed (${integrity.reason}); run advisor_rebuild`);\n434:     }\n435:     const sourceScan = scanSkillMetadataFiles(skillRoot, args.maxMetadataFiles ?? DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES);\n436:     if (sourceScan.truncated) {\n437:       errors.push(`advisor_status metadata scan capped at ${sourceScan.count} files`);\n438:     }\n439:     const indexStaleness = readIndexStaleness(dbPath, workspaceRoot);\n440:     if (indexStaleness.state === 'stale') {\n441:       const staleSkillCount = indexStaleness.changedSourceFiles + indexStaleness.missingSourceFiles;\n442:       errors.push(\n443:         `advisor_status index content hashes differ from disk for ${staleSkillCount} skill${staleSkillCount === 1 ? '' : 's'}; run advisor_rebuild`,\n444:       );\n445:     }\n446:     const sourceChanged = generation.state === 'stale'\n447:       || indexStaleness.state === 'stale'\n448:       || (\n449:         generation.sourceSignature\n450:           ? computeAdvisorSourceSignature(workspaceRoot) !== generation.sourceSignature\n451:           : hasArtifact && hasSources && sourceScan.maxMtimeMs > fileMtimeMs(dbPath)\n452:       );\n453:     const daemonPid = parseDaemonPid();\n454:     const daemonAvailable = daemonPid === undefined ? true : hasRunningDaemon(daemonPid);\n455:     // Only flag a daemon-evidence divergence when a PID file exists but the\n456:     // process is gone. Missing PID file = daemon never started, not a\n457:     // divergence between freshness artifacts and live process evidence.\n458:     if (daemonPid !== undefined && !daemonAvailable && generation.state !== 'unavailable') {\n459:       errors.push('advisor_status found freshness artifacts, but no live daemon PID/process evidence');\n460:     }\n461:     const state = isFreshness(generation.state) ? generation.state : 'unavailable';\n462:     // Data is stale when sources are physically newer than the\n463:     // artifact, regardless of stored sourceSignature semantics. This is the\n464:     // stronger physical-evidence signal vs. signature mismatch which can\n465:     // arise from benign workspace differences.\n466:     const sourcesNewerThanArtifact = hasArtifact && hasSources\n467:       && sourceScan.maxMtimeMs > fileMtimeMs(dbPath);\n468:     const trustState = createTrustState({\n469:       hasSources,\n470:       hasArtifact,\n471:       sourceChanged,\n472:       daemonAvailable,\n473:       generation: generation.generation,\n474:       reason: generation.reason,\n475:       lastLiveAt: state === 'live' ? generation.updatedAt : null,\n476:     });\n477:     // `freshness` describes data/artifact state (live/stale/absent/\n478:     // unavailable from the generation file), while `trustState.state` is the\n479:     // daemon-gated caller-trust axis. Keep them decoupled so callers reading\n480:     // `freshness` see artifact health independent of daemon availability.\n481:     // When physical evidence shows sources are newer than the DB, downgrade\n482:     // a 'live' generation to 'stale' regardless of signature noise.\n483:     const freshnessOutput: AdvisorFreshness = state === 'live'\n484:       && (sourceChanged || artifactCorrupt || (!generation.sourceSignature && sourcesNewerThanArtifact))\n485:       ? 'stale'\n486:       : state;\n487:     const hookHealthSection = readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot);\n488:     const output: AdvisorStatusOutput = {\n489:       freshness: freshnessOutput,\n490:       generation: generation.generation,\n491:       trustState,\n492:       lastGenerationBump: generation.updatedAt === new Date(0).toISOString() ? null : generation.updatedAt,\n493:       lastScanAt: generation.updatedAt === new Date(0).toISOString() ? null : generation.updatedAt,\n494:       skillCount: sourceScan.count,\n495:       indexStaleness,\n496:       laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,\n497:       // The p95 counts cache-hit invocations only, because a miss pays the\n498:       // child-process cost that the alert thresholds are not set against.\n499:       ...(hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length > 0\n500:         ? {\n501:             hookHealth: {\n502:               invocations: hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length,\n503:               rollingP95Ms: hookHealthSection.rollingP95Ms,\n504:               rollingFailOpenRate: hookHealthSection.rollingFailOpenRate,\n505:               rollingCacheHitRate: hookHealthSection.rollingCacheHitRate,\n506:             },\n507:           }\n508:         : {}),\n509:       ...((args.includeSemanticHealth || args.debug) ? { semanticLaneHealth: readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath) } : {}),\n510:       ...(daemonPid ? { daemonPid } : {}),\n511:       ...(errors.length > 0 ? { errors } : {}),\n512:     };\n513:     return AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse(output);\n514:   } catch (error: unknown) {\n515:     const message = redactDiagnosticText(errorMessage(error));\n516:     const sourceScan = scanSkillMetadataFiles(skillRoot, args.maxMetadataFiles ?? DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES);\n517:     const trustState = createTrustState({\n518:       hasSources: existsSync(skillRoot),\n519:       hasArtifact: existsSync(dbPath),\n520:       sourceChanged: false,\n521:       daemonAvailable: false,\n522:       generation: 0,\n523:       reason: 'ADVISOR_STATUS_UNAVAILABLE',\n524:     });\n525:     const output: AdvisorStatusOutput = {\n526:       freshness: 'unavailable',\n527:       generation: 0,\n528:       trustState,\n529:       lastGenerationBump: null,\n530:       lastScanAt: null,\n531:       skillCount: sourceScan.count,\n532:       laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,\n533:       ...((args.includeSemanticHealth || args.debug) ? { semanticLaneHealth: readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath) } : {}),\n534:       errors: [message],\n535:     };\n536:     return AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse(output);\n537:   }\n538: }\n539: \n540: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n541: // 5. EXPORTS\n542: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n543: \n544: /** Handle the advisor_status command request. */\n545: export async function handleAdvisorStatus(args: unknown): Promise<HandlerResponse> {\n546:   // The diagnostic surface opts into the artifact integrity probe by default\n547:   // so operators see on-disk corruption; explicit input can still override it.\n548:   const parsed = AdvisorStatusInputSchema.parse(args);\n549:   const status = readAdvisorStatus({ ...parsed, checkArtifactIntegrity: parsed.checkArtifactIntegrity ?? true });\n550:   const withBackend = parsed.includeSemanticHealth === true && status.semanticLaneHealth\n551:     ? { ...status, semanticLaneHealth: await probeSemanticLaneBackend(status.semanticLaneHealth) }\n552:     : status;\n553:   // Keep the bounded probe on this async command path, away from the synchronous recommend reader.\n554:   const data = parsed.includeEmbeddingsHealth === true\n555:     ? AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse({ ...withBackend, embeddingsHealth: await readEmbeddingsHealth() })\n556:     : withBackend;\n557:   return {\n558:     content: [{\n559:       type: 'text',\n560:       text: JSON.stringify({ status: 'ok', data }, null, 2),\n561:     }],\n562:   };\n563: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts, lines 1-563\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: advisor_status Handler\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\n10: import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n11: import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n12: \n13: import { computeAdvisorSourceSignature } from '../lib/freshness.js';\n14: import { readSkillGraphGeneration } from '../lib/freshness/generation.js';\n15: import { checkSqliteIntegrity } from '../lib/freshness/sqlite-integrity.js';\n16: import { createPrivateSkillLinkCheck } from '../lib/private-skill-target.js';\n17: import {\n18:   computeSkillMetadataContentHash,\n19:   isGenuineCorruptionReason,\n20:   readCommandEmbeddingSources,\n21:   resolveSkillGraphDbDir,\n22:   DB_FILENAME,\n23: } from '../lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js';\n24: import { createTrustState } from '../lib/freshness/trust-state.js';\n25: import { getAdapter, getManifest } from '../lib/embedders/registry.js';\n26: import { probeOllamaModel, resolveOllamaBaseUrl } from '../lib/embedders/adapters/ollama.js';\n27: import { commandVecTableNameForDim } from '../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n28: import { readEmbeddingsHealth } from '../lib/embedders/embeddings-health.js';\n29: import { getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth } from '../lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js';\n30: import { readAdvisorEmbeddingStaleness } from '../lib/scorer/projection.js';\n31: import { DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS } from '../lib/scorer/weights-config.js';\n32: import { readAdvisorHookHealthSection } from '../lib/metrics.js';\n33: import { errorMessage } from '../lib/utils/error-format.js';\n34: import { redactDiagnosticText } from './skill-graph/response-envelope.js';\n35: import {\n36:   AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n37:   AdvisorStatusOutputSchema,\n38: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n39: \n40: import type {\n41:   AdvisorFreshness,\n42:   AdvisorStatusInput,\n43:   AdvisorStatusOutput,\n44: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n45: \n46: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n47: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS AND CONSTANTS\n48: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: \n50: type HandlerResponse = { content: Array<{ type: string; text: string }> };\n51: type IndexStaleness = NonNullable<AdvisorStatusOutput['indexStaleness']>;\n52: \n53: const SKILL_ROOT = join('.skilled', 'skills');\n54: const DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES = 5_000;\n55: type SemanticLaneHealth = NonNullable<AdvisorStatusOutput['semanticLaneHealth']>;\n56: \n57: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: // 3. HELPERS\n59: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n60: \n61: function isFreshness(value: string): value is AdvisorFreshness {\n62:   return value === 'live' || value === 'stale' || value === 'absent' || value === 'unavailable';\n63: }\n64: \n65: function parseDaemonPid(): number | undefined {\n66:   const raw = process.env.SPECKIT_SKILL_GRAPH_DAEMON_PID;\n67:   if (!raw) return undefined;\n68:   const parsed = Number(raw);\n69:   return Number.isSafeInteger(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : undefined;\n70: }\n71: \n72: function hasRunningDaemon(pid: number | undefined): boolean {\n73:   if (!pid) {\n74:     return false;\n75:   }\n76:   try {\n77:     process.kill(pid, 0);\n78:     return true;\n79:   } catch {\n80:     return false;\n81:   }\n82: }\n83: \n84: function fileMtimeMs(path: string): number {\n85:   if (!existsSync(path)) return 0;\n86:   const stat = statSync(path);\n87:   return stat.mtimeMs;\n88: }\n89: \n90: function resolveSkillGraphDbPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n91:   // Resolve through the writer's own resolver so the integrity probe always\n92:   // targets the exact file the daemon writes. An env override wins for both;\n93:   // otherwise the workspace root stands in for the writer's cwd, which match\n94:   // in the normal single-root deployment.\n95:   return join(resolveSkillGraphDbDir(workspaceRoot), DB_FILENAME);\n96: }\n97: \n98: // Per-(dbPath, generation, mtime) integrity verdict cache. A full quick_check\n99: // scans the artifact, which is too costly to run on the recommend hot path;\n100: // caching it lets recommend opt into corruption detection while paying the\n101: // scan at most once per generation. The only events that can change on-disk\n102: // integrity — a generation bump or an mtime change — invalidate the entry.\n103: const integrityVerdictCache = new Map<string, { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string }>();\n104: \n105: function checkSqliteIntegrityCached(\n106:   dbPath: string,\n107:   generation: number,\n108:   mtimeMs: number,\n109: ): { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string } {\n110:   const key = `${dbPath}::${generation}::${mtimeMs}`;\n111:   const cached = integrityVerdictCache.get(key);\n112:   if (cached) {\n113:     return cached;\n114:   }\n115:   const result = checkSqliteIntegrity(dbPath);\n116:   // Only the newest (path, generation, mtime) verdict is ever consulted, so a\n117:   // single-entry cache is sufficient and self-bounding.\n118:   integrityVerdictCache.clear();\n119:   integrityVerdictCache.set(key, result);\n120:   return result;\n121: }\n122: \n123: function tableExists(database: Database.Database, tableName: string): boolean {\n124:   const row = database.prepare(`\n125:     SELECT 1 AS present\n126:     FROM sqlite_master\n127:     WHERE type = 'table' AND name = ?\n128:     LIMIT 1\n129:   `).get(tableName) as { present: number } | undefined;\n130:   return Boolean(row);\n131: }\n132: \n133: function metadataValue(database: Database.Database, key: string): string | null {\n134:   if (!tableExists(database, 'vec_metadata')) return null;\n135:   const row = database.prepare('SELECT value FROM vec_metadata WHERE key = ?').get(key) as { value: string } | undefined;\n136:   return row?.value ?? null;\n137: }\n138: \n139: function countRows(database: Database.Database, sql: string): number {\n140:   const row = database.prepare(sql).get() as { c: number } | undefined;\n141:   return row?.c ?? 0;\n142: }\n143: \n144: function maxUpdatedAt(database: Database.Database, tableName: string): string | null {\n145:   const row = database.prepare(`SELECT MAX(updated_at) AS updatedAt FROM ${tableName}`).get() as { updatedAt: string | null } | undefined;\n146:   return row?.updatedAt ?? null;\n147: }\n148: \n149: function baseSemanticLaneHealth(disabledReason: string | null): SemanticLaneHealth {\n150:   return {\n151:     activeEmbedder: null,\n152:     vectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: 0, ratio: 0 },\n153:     dimMismatch: false,\n154:     lastRefresh: null,\n155:     disabledReason,\n156:     laneEnabled: false,\n157:     checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n158:   };\n159: }\n160: \n161: function readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath: string): SemanticLaneHealth {\n162:   const runtime = getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth();\n163:   // The command projection's size does not depend on the database, so the\n164:   // denominator is known even when the artifact is missing or unreadable.\n165:   const commandTotal = readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0;\n166:   if (!existsSync(dbPath)) {\n167:     return {\n168:       ...baseSemanticLaneHealth(runtime.disabledReason ?? 'database_absent'),\n169:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: commandTotal },\n170:     };\n171:   }\n172: \n173:   let database: Database.Database | null = null;\n174:   try {\n175:     database = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n176:     const total = tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes')\n177:       ? countRows(database, 'SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM skill_nodes')\n178:       : 0;\n179:     const activeName = metadataValue(database, 'active_embedder_name');\n180:     const activeDimRaw = metadataValue(database, 'active_embedder_dim');\n181:     const activeDim = activeDimRaw ? Number.parseInt(activeDimRaw, 10) : 0;\n182:     const hasActive = Boolean(activeName) && Number.isInteger(activeDim) && activeDim > 0;\n183:     const adapter = activeName ? getAdapter(activeName) : undefined;\n184:     const activeEmbedder = activeName\n185:       ? { name: activeName, dim: Number.isInteger(activeDim) && activeDim > 0 ? activeDim : 0, adapterDim: adapter?.dim ?? null }\n186:       : null;\n187:     const tableName = hasActive ? `vec_${activeDim}` : null;\n188:     const hasVecTable = tableName ? tableExists(database, tableName) : false;\n189:     const embedded = hasVecTable\n190:       ? countRows(database, `SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM ${tableName} WHERE embedding IS NOT NULL`)\n191:       : (tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes') ? countRows(database, 'SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM skill_nodes WHERE embedding IS NOT NULL') : 0);\n192:     const lastRefresh = hasVecTable && tableName ? maxUpdatedAt(database, tableName) : null;\n193:     const commandTable = hasActive ? commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim) : null;\n194:     const commandEmbedded = commandTable && tableExists(database, commandTable)\n195:       ? countRows(database, `SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM ${commandTable}`)\n196:       : 0;\n197:     const dimMismatch = Boolean(activeEmbedder && activeEmbedder.adapterDim !== null && activeEmbedder.dim !== activeEmbedder.adapterDim);\n198:     const staleness = readAdvisorEmbeddingStaleness(database);\n199:     const disabledReason = dimMismatch\n200:       ? 'dim_mismatch'\n201:       : (staleness.stale\n202:           ? 'projection_embedding_stale'\n203:           : (!hasActive\n204:               ? 'active_embedder_unset'\n205:               : (!adapter\n206:                   ? 'adapter_unavailable'\n207:                   : (!hasVecTable\n208:                       ? 'vector_table_missing'\n209:                       : (total > 0 && embedded === 0 ? 'no_skill_vectors' : runtime.disabledReason)))));\n210:     return {\n211:       activeEmbedder,\n212:       vectorCoverage: {\n213:         embedded,\n214:         total,\n215:         ratio: total > 0 ? Math.round((embedded / total) * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000 : 0,\n216:       },\n217:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: commandEmbedded, total: commandTotal },\n218:       dimMismatch,\n219:       lastRefresh,\n220:       disabledReason,\n221:       laneEnabled: Boolean(hasActive && adapter && !dimMismatch && !staleness.stale && hasVecTable && embedded > 0 && !disabledReason),\n222:       checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n223:     };\n224:   } catch {\n225:     return {\n226:       ...baseSemanticLaneHealth(runtime.disabledReason ?? 'health_unavailable'),\n227:       commandVectorCoverage: { embedded: 0, total: commandTotal },\n228:     };\n229:   } finally {\n230:     database?.close();\n231:   }\n232: }\n233: \n234: function readIndexStaleness(dbPath: string, workspaceRoot: string): IndexStaleness {\n235:   const unavailable = (reason: string): IndexStaleness => ({\n236:     state: 'unavailable',\n237:     reason,\n238:     trackedSkills: 0,\n239:     freshSourceFiles: 0,\n240:     changedSourceFiles: 0,\n241:     missingSourceFiles: 0,\n242:     staleSkillIds: [],\n243:   });\n244:   if (!existsSync(dbPath)) return unavailable('database_absent');\n245: \n246:   let database: Database.Database | null = null;\n247:   let result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n248:   try {\n249:     database = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n250:     if (!tableExists(database, 'skill_nodes')) {\n251:       result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n252:     } else {\n253:       const columns = database.pragma('table_info(skill_nodes)') as Array<{ name: string }>;\n254:       const hasSourceColumns = columns.some((column) => column.name === 'source_path')\n255:         && columns.some((column) => column.name === 'content_hash');\n256:       if (!hasSourceColumns) {\n257:         result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n258:       } else {\n259:         const rows = database.prepare(`\n260:           SELECT id, source_path, content_hash\n261:           FROM skill_nodes\n262:           ORDER BY id\n263:         `).all() as Array<{\n264:           id: string;\n265:           source_path: string | null;\n266:           content_hash: string | null;\n267:         }>;\n268:         if (rows.length === 0) {\n269:           result = unavailable('index_rows_absent');\n270:         } else {\n271:           let freshSourceFiles = 0;\n272:           let changedSourceFiles = 0;\n273:           let missingSourceFiles = 0;\n274:           const staleSkillIds: string[] = [];\n275: \n276:           for (const row of rows) {\n277:             if (!row.source_path || row.source_path.trim().length === 0) {\n278:               missingSourceFiles++;\n279:               staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n280:               continue;\n281:             }\n282: \n283:             let content: string;\n284:             try {\n285:               content = readFileSync(resolve(workspaceRoot, row.source_path), 'utf8');\n286:             } catch (error: unknown) {\n287:               if (error instanceof Error && 'code' in error && error.code === 'ENOENT') {\n288:                 missingSourceFiles++;\n289:                 staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n290:                 continue;\n291:               }\n292:               throw error;\n293:             }\n294: \n295:             if (row.content_hash === null\n296:               || computeSkillMetadataContentHash(content) !== row.content_hash) {\n297:               changedSourceFiles++;\n298:               staleSkillIds.push(row.id);\n299:               continue;\n300:             }\n301: \n302:             freshSourceFiles++;\n303:           }\n304: \n305:           const stale = changedSourceFiles + missingSourceFiles > 0;\n306:           result = {\n307:             state: stale ? 'stale' : 'fresh',\n308:             reason: stale ? 'source_hash_mismatch' : null,\n309:             trackedSkills: rows.length,\n310:             freshSourceFiles,\n311:             changedSourceFiles,\n312:             missingSourceFiles,\n313:             staleSkillIds: staleSkillIds.slice(0, 25),\n314:           };\n315:         }\n316:       }\n317:     }\n318:   } catch {\n319:     result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n320:   } finally {\n321:     try {\n322:       database?.close();\n323:     } catch {\n324:       result = unavailable('index_read_failed');\n325:     }\n326:   }\n327: \n328:   return result;\n329: }\n330: \n331: function scanSkillMetadataFiles(\n332:   skillRoot: string,\n333:   maxFiles = DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES,\n334: ): { count: number; maxMtimeMs: number; truncated: boolean } {\n335:   if (!existsSync(skillRoot)) return { count: 0, maxMtimeMs: 0, truncated: false };\n336:   const isTrustedLink = createPrivateSkillLinkCheck(skillRoot);\n337:   const skillRoots = readdirSync(skillRoot, { withFileTypes: true })\n338:     .filter((entry) => !entry.name.startsWith('.') && (entry.isDirectory()\n339:       || (entry.name.startsWith('local-')\n340:         && entry.isSymbolicLink()\n341:         && isTrustedLink(join(skillRoot, entry.name)))))\n342:     .sort((left, right) => left.name.localeCompare(right.name));\n343:   let count = 0;\n344:   let newest = 0;\n345:   let truncated = false;\n346:   for (const entry of skillRoots) {\n347:     const metadataPath = join(skillRoot, entry.name, 'graph-metadata.json');\n348:     if (!existsSync(metadataPath)) continue;\n349:     const metadataStat = statSync(metadataPath);\n350:     if (!metadataStat.isFile()) continue;\n351:     if (count >= maxFiles) {\n352:       truncated = true;\n353:       break;\n354:     }\n355:     count++;\n356:     newest = Math.max(newest, metadataStat.mtimeMs);\n357:   }\n358:   return { count, maxMtimeMs: newest, truncated };\n359: }\n360: \n361: // The status reader stays synchronous so the recommend path can call it, which\n362: // puts the only network probe here on the async command path. Reading /api/tags\n363: // is the only signal that separates a stopped server or a missing model from a\n364: // healthy lane: the pointer and the vectors survive both, so a lane that\n365: // reports enabled through an outage sends operators to rebuild a fine index\n366: // instead of starting the server.\n367: async function probeSemanticLaneBackend(health: SemanticLaneHealth): Promise<SemanticLaneHealth> {\n368:   const activeName = health.activeEmbedder?.name;\n369:   const manifest = activeName ? getManifest(activeName) : undefined;\n370:   if (!manifest) {\n371:     return health;\n372:   }\n373:   if (manifest.backend !== 'ollama') {\n374:     return {\n375:       ...health,\n376:       backend: { state: 'probe_not_implemented', reason: `no readiness probe for the ${manifest.backend} backend` },\n377:       laneEnabled: false,\n378:     };\n379:   }\n380:   const probe = await probeOllamaModel(\n381:     resolveOllamaBaseUrl(),\n382:     manifest.ollamaName ?? manifest.name,\n383:     500,\n384:   );\n385:   if (probe.available) {\n386:     return { ...health, backend: { state: 'reachable', reason: null } };\n387:   }\n388:   const reason = probe.reason ?? null;\n389:   return {\n390:     ...health,\n391:     backend: {\n392:       state: reason && /not loaded/i.test(reason) ? 'model_missing' : 'unreachable',\n393:       reason,\n394:     },\n395:     laneEnabled: false,\n396:   };\n397: }\n398: \n399: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n400: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n401: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n402: \n403: /** Read advisor freshness state.\n404:  *\n405:  * Diagnostic-only: this function reports stale, absent, or unavailable advisor\n406:  * state and does not rebuild it. Use `advisor_rebuild` to repair stale state.\n407:  */\n408: export function readAdvisorStatus(input: AdvisorStatusInput): AdvisorStatusOutput {\n409:   const args = AdvisorStatusInputSchema.parse(input);\n410:   const workspaceRoot = resolve(args.workspaceRoot);\n411:   const dbPath = resolveSkillGraphDbPath(workspaceRoot);\n412:   const skillRoot = join(workspaceRoot, SKILL_ROOT);\n413:   const errors: string[] = [];\n414: \n415:   try {\n416:     const generation = readSkillGraphGeneration(workspaceRoot);\n417:     const hasSources = existsSync(skillRoot);\n418:     const hasArtifact = existsSync(dbPath);\n419:     // Existence alone lets a corrupt-on-disk artifact report 'live' from the\n420:     // generation counters, which makes advisor_rebuild skip the repair it\n421:     // exists to perform. A read-only quick_check turns genuine corruption\n422:     // into a stale signal so rebuild runs. Transient lock/IO failures are\n423:     // excluded so contention never forces a spurious rebuild.\n424:     const integrity = (hasArtifact && args.checkArtifactIntegrity === true)\n425:       ? checkSqliteIntegrityCached(dbPath, generation.generation, fileMtimeMs(dbPath))\n426:       : null;\n427:     const artifactCorrupt = Boolean(\n428:       integrity && !integrity.ok\n429:         && integrity.reason !== 'SQLITE_ABSENT'\n430:         && isGenuineCorruptionReason(integrity.reason),\n431:     );\n432:     if (artifactCorrupt && integrity && !integrity.ok) {\n433:       errors.push(`advisor_status skill graph integrity check failed (${integrity.reason}); run advisor_rebuild`);\n434:     }\n435:     const sourceScan = scanSkillMetadataFiles(skillRoot, args.maxMetadataFiles ?? DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES);\n436:     if (sourceScan.truncated) {\n437:       errors.push(`advisor_status metadata scan capped at ${sourceScan.count} files`);\n438:     }\n439:     const indexStaleness = readIndexStaleness(dbPath, workspaceRoot);\n440:     if (indexStaleness.state === 'stale') {\n441:       const staleSkillCount = indexStaleness.changedSourceFiles + indexStaleness.missingSourceFiles;\n442:       errors.push(\n443:         `advisor_status index content hashes differ from disk for ${staleSkillCount} skill${staleSkillCount === 1 ? '' : 's'}; run advisor_rebuild`,\n444:       );\n445:     }\n446:     const sourceChanged = generation.state === 'stale'\n447:       || indexStaleness.state === 'stale'\n448:       || (\n449:         generation.sourceSignature\n450:           ? computeAdvisorSourceSignature(workspaceRoot) !== generation.sourceSignature\n451:           : hasArtifact && hasSources && sourceScan.maxMtimeMs > fileMtimeMs(dbPath)\n452:       );\n453:     const daemonPid = parseDaemonPid();\n454:     const daemonAvailable = daemonPid === undefined ? true : hasRunningDaemon(daemonPid);\n455:     // Only flag a daemon-evidence divergence when a PID file exists but the\n456:     // process is gone. Missing PID file = daemon never started, not a\n457:     // divergence between freshness artifacts and live process evidence.\n458:     if (daemonPid !== undefined && !daemonAvailable && generation.state !== 'unavailable') {\n459:       errors.push('advisor_status found freshness artifacts, but no live daemon PID/process evidence');\n460:     }\n461:     const state = isFreshness(generation.state) ? generation.state : 'unavailable';\n462:     // Data is stale when sources are physically newer than the\n463:     // artifact, regardless of stored sourceSignature semantics. This is the\n464:     // stronger physical-evidence signal vs. signature mismatch which can\n465:     // arise from benign workspace differences.\n466:     const sourcesNewerThanArtifact = hasArtifact && hasSources\n467:       && sourceScan.maxMtimeMs > fileMtimeMs(dbPath);\n468:     const trustState = createTrustState({\n469:       hasSources,\n470:       hasArtifact,\n471:       sourceChanged,\n472:       daemonAvailable,\n473:       generation: generation.generation,\n474:       reason: generation.reason,\n475:       lastLiveAt: state === 'live' ? generation.updatedAt : null,\n476:     });\n477:     // `freshness` describes data/artifact state (live/stale/absent/\n478:     // unavailable from the generation file), while `trustState.state` is the\n479:     // daemon-gated caller-trust axis. Keep them decoupled so callers reading\n480:     // `freshness` see artifact health independent of daemon availability.\n481:     // When physical evidence shows sources are newer than the DB, downgrade\n482:     // a 'live' generation to 'stale' regardless of signature noise.\n483:     const freshnessOutput: AdvisorFreshness = state === 'live'\n484:       && (sourceChanged || artifactCorrupt || (!generation.sourceSignature && sourcesNewerThanArtifact))\n485:       ? 'stale'\n486:       : state;\n487:     const hookHealthSection = readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot);\n488:     const output: AdvisorStatusOutput = {\n489:       freshness: freshnessOutput,\n490:       generation: generation.generation,\n491:       trustState,\n492:       lastGenerationBump: generation.updatedAt === new Date(0).toISOString() ? null : generation.updatedAt,\n493:       lastScanAt: generation.updatedAt === new Date(0).toISOString() ? null : generation.updatedAt,\n494:       skillCount: sourceScan.count,\n495:       indexStaleness,\n496:       laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,\n497:       // The p95 counts cache-hit invocations only, because a miss pays the\n498:       // child-process cost that the alert thresholds are not set against.\n499:       ...(hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length > 0\n500:         ? {\n501:             hookHealth: {\n502:               invocations: hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length,\n503:               rollingP95Ms: hookHealthSection.rollingP95Ms,\n504:               rollingFailOpenRate: hookHealthSection.rollingFailOpenRate,\n505:               rollingCacheHitRate: hookHealthSection.rollingCacheHitRate,\n506:             },\n507:           }\n508:         : {}),\n509:       ...((args.includeSemanticHealth || args.debug) ? { semanticLaneHealth: readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath) } : {}),\n510:       ...(daemonPid ? { daemonPid } : {}),\n511:       ...(errors.length > 0 ? { errors } : {}),\n512:     };\n513:     return AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse(output);\n514:   } catch (error: unknown) {\n515:     const message = redactDiagnosticText(errorMessage(error));\n516:     const sourceScan = scanSkillMetadataFiles(skillRoot, args.maxMetadataFiles ?? DEFAULT_MAX_METADATA_FILES);\n517:     const trustState = createTrustState({\n518:       hasSources: existsSync(skillRoot),\n519:       hasArtifact: existsSync(dbPath),\n520:       sourceChanged: false,\n521:       daemonAvailable: false,\n522:       generation: 0,\n523:       reason: 'ADVISOR_STATUS_UNAVAILABLE',\n524:     });\n525:     const output: AdvisorStatusOutput = {\n526:       freshness: 'unavailable',\n527:       generation: 0,\n528:       trustState,\n529:       lastGenerationBump: null,\n530:       lastScanAt: null,\n531:       skillCount: sourceScan.count,\n532:       laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,\n533:       ...((args.includeSemanticHealth || args.debug) ? { semanticLaneHealth: readSemanticLaneHealth(dbPath) } : {}),\n534:       errors: [message],\n535:     };\n536:     return AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse(output);\n537:   }\n538: }\n539: \n540: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n541: // 5. EXPORTS\n542: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n543: \n544: /** Handle the advisor_status command request. */\n545: export async function handleAdvisorStatus(args: unknown): Promise<HandlerResponse> {\n546:   // The diagnostic surface opts into the artifact integrity probe by default\n547:   // so operators see on-disk corruption; explicit input can still override it.\n548:   const parsed = AdvisorStatusInputSchema.parse(args);\n549:   const status = readAdvisorStatus({ ...parsed, checkArtifactIntegrity: parsed.checkArtifactIntegrity ?? true });\n550:   const withBackend = parsed.includeSemanticHealth === true && status.semanticLaneHealth\n551:     ? { ...status, semanticLaneHealth: await probeSemanticLaneBackend(status.semanticLaneHealth) }\n552:     : status;\n553:   // Keep the bounded probe on this async command path, away from the synchronous recommend reader.\n554:   const data = parsed.includeEmbeddingsHealth === true\n555:     ? AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse({ ...withBackend, embeddingsHealth: await readEmbeddingsHealth() })\n556:     : withBackend;\n557:   return {\n558:     content: [{\n559:       type: 'text',\n560:       text: JSON.stringify({ status: 'ok', data }, null, 2),\n561:     }],\n562:   };\n563: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794565099181,"end":1794565100002}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794565100007,"sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d46a5031001ERW4gvHa5Jf04t","sessionID":"ses_e2b9698caffeLgfL2URRQHee3D","messageID":"msg_1d46a36f0001uHMu5b0qbKGqrh","type":"tool","id":"call_f17cd0ce356643749d8452e5","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts, lines 1-654\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Tool Schemas\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { z } from 'zod';\n10: import { existsSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES } from '../lib/advisor-runtime-values.js';\n14: import { SCORER_LANE_IDS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n15: \n16: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17: // 2. CONSTANTS\n18: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: \n20: export const AdvisorFreshnessSchema = z.enum(['live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable']);\n21: export const AdvisorLaneSchema = z.enum(SCORER_LANE_IDS);\n22: \n23: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: // 3. HELPERS\n25: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n26: \n27: // Bound caller-supplied workspaceRoot inputs to a small\n28: // allowlist (repo root + os.tmpdir()) so handlers cannot be coerced into\n29: // resolving paths outside the workspace. resolve() canonicalizes the input\n30: // path; realpathSync follows symlinks; the prefix check rejects anything\n31: // that escapes the allowlist after canonicalization.\n32: //\n33: // Directory names the source tree may sit under. A checkout may link one to the\n34: // other, so both mark the same tree.\n35: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n36: \n37: // Repo root is detected by walking up from process.cwd() looking for the\n38: // system-spec-kit SKILL.md sentinel — same shape as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot but\n39: // inlined here to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/. The start\n40: // directory is a parameter so the lockstep test can feed both resolvers one tree.\n41: export function detectRepoRoot(start: string = process.cwd()): string {\n42:   // Use the same SKILL.md file sentinel as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot so the schema\n43:   // and the handler agree on which directory is the workspace root. A bare\n44:   // directory sentinel would match the nested mock trees other workflows create.\n45:   // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, so the sentinel is\n46:   // tested under both.\n47:   const sentinels = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => `${name}/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`);\n48:   let current = resolve(start);\n49:   for (let index = 0; index < 14; index += 1) {\n50:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n51:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n52:     if (parent === current) break;\n53:     current = parent;\n54:   }\n55:   // Lockstep with findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot: when the walk misses the sentinel,\n56:   // never anchor the allowlist on a directory inside a source tree. Take the start\n57:   // or the nearest source-root parent that holds the sentinel, else hoist above the\n58:   // outermost source-root segment, so caller-supplied workspaceRoots are bounded\n59:   // to the real root, not a nested subdir.\n60:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n61: }\n62: \n63: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:nearestSentinelHolder, kept local for\n64: // the same reason as the hoist below. A capped walk misses the sentinel, yet the root\n65: // is still the start or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path, so\n66: // testing the start and then those parents nearest first keeps a repository that\n67: // sits under a directory named .skilled or .opencode.\n68: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n69:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n70:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n71:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n72:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n73:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n74:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n75:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n76:   }\n77:   return null;\n78: }\n79: \n80: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:hoistAboveOpencodeTree. Kept local\n81: // to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/ — the two must stay in\n82: // lockstep so the schema allowlist and the handler agree on the workspace root.\n83: // A `.skilled` or `.opencode` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n84: // root, so hoisting above the OUTERMOST one yields the real root and can never\n85: // return a path inside a source tree (the earlier specs-only shape missed sibling\n86: // subtrees like skills/).\n87: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n88:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n89:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n90:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n91:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n92:     }\n93:   }\n94:   return null;\n95: }\n96: \n97: function canonicalize(input: string): string {\n98:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n99:   try {\n100:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n101:   } catch {\n102:     // Path may not exist yet (test fixtures created lazily,\n103:     // tmpdir mkdtemp paths probed before mkdir). Walk up and realpath the\n104:     // first existing ancestor, then re-join the unresolved tail. This\n105:     // resolves macOS-style symlinks like /tmp → /private/tmp even when\n106:     // the leaf doesn't exist.\n107:     let probe = resolved;\n108:     let tail = '';\n109:     for (let depth = 0; depth < 32; depth += 1) {\n110:       const parent = resolve(probe, '..');\n111:       if (parent === probe) break;\n112:       try {\n113:         const realParent = realpathSync.native(parent);\n114:         return tail\n115:           ? resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1) + tail)\n116:           : resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1));\n117:       } catch {\n118:         // Parent doesn't exist either — keep walking up.\n119:         const segment = probe.slice(parent.length + 1);\n120:         tail = tail ? `${segment}/${tail}` : segment;\n121:         probe = parent;\n122:       }\n123:     }\n124:     return resolved;\n125:   }\n126: }\n127: \n128: const SOURCE_REPO_ROOT = canonicalize(detectRepoRoot());\n129: \n130: const ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES: readonly string[] = (() => {\n131:   const prefixes: string[] = [];\n132:   prefixes.push(SOURCE_REPO_ROOT);\n133:   prefixes.push(canonicalize(tmpdir()));\n134:   // Include the canonicalized /tmp prefix as well. On macOS\n135:   // os.tmpdir() returns the per-user temp dir under /var/folders/...; the\n136:   // /tmp symlink resolves to /private/tmp. Test fixtures and tools that\n137:   // hardcode /tmp/foo paths need both forms in the allowlist.\n138:   prefixes.push(canonicalize('/tmp'));\n139:   // Accept additional explicit allowlist via env (CI / test runners).\n140:   const envExtras = process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST;\n141:   if (envExtras) {\n142:     for (const extra of envExtras.split(':')) {\n143:       const trimmed = extra.trim();\n144:       if (trimmed) prefixes.push(canonicalize(trimmed));\n145:     }\n146:   }\n147:   return Array.from(new Set(prefixes));\n148: })();\n149: \n150: /**\n151:  * Validate that a caller-supplied workspaceRoot resolves under\n152:  * the repo root, os.tmpdir(), or an explicit allowlist entry after\n153:  * realpath canonicalization.\n154:  *\n155:  * Exported so handlers can re-canonicalize at call time and reuse the\n156:  * same bounding logic the schema applies at parse time.\n157:  */\n158: export function isAllowedWorkspaceRoot(input: string): boolean {\n159:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n160:   const canonical = canonicalize(input);\n161:   return ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES.some(\n162:     (prefix) => canonical === prefix || canonical.startsWith(`${prefix}/`),\n163:   ) || isWiredToSourceTree(canonical);\n164: }\n165: \n166: function realpathOrNull(path: string): string | null {\n167:   try {\n168:     return realpathSync.native(path);\n169:   } catch {\n170:     return null;\n171:   }\n172: }\n173: \n174: /**\n175:  * True when the input, or a directory above it, holds a source-root entry\n176:  * (`.skilled` or `.opencode`) whose realpath is the source tree's own entry.\n177:  *\n178:  * A project linked to a shared checkout holds `.skilled -> <source>/.skilled`\n179:  * while the daemon runs from the source tree, so the prefix allowlist alone\n180:  * refuses every linked project. Matching realpaths admits only a workspace that\n181:  * is actually wired to this source; a copied tree or a link to another source\n182:  * resolves elsewhere and stays refused.\n183:  */\n184: export function isWiredToSourceTree(input: string, sourceRoot: string = SOURCE_REPO_ROOT): boolean {\n185:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n186:   const sourceEntries = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES\n187:     .map((name) => realpathOrNull(resolve(sourceRoot, name)))\n188:     .filter((entry): entry is string => entry !== null);\n189:   if (sourceEntries.length === 0) return false;\n190:   let current = canonicalize(input);\n191:   for (let depth = 0; depth < 64; depth += 1) {\n192:     for (const name of SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES) {\n193:       const entry = realpathOrNull(resolve(current, name));\n194:       if (entry !== null && sourceEntries.includes(entry)) return true;\n195:     }\n196:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n197:     if (parent === current) break;\n198:     current = parent;\n199:   }\n200:   return false;\n201: }\n202: \n203: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n204: // 4. SCHEMA DEFINITIONS\n205: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n206: \n207: const BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema = z\n208:   .string()\n209:   .min(1)\n210:   .refine(isAllowedWorkspaceRoot, {\n211:     message:\n212:       'workspaceRoot must resolve under the repo root, os.tmpdir(), an explicit SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST entry, or a project whose .skilled links to this source tree',\n213:   });\n214: \n215: const laneBreakdownSchema = z.object({\n216:   lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n217:   rawScore: z.number().min(0),\n218:   weightedScore: z.number().min(0),\n219:   weight: z.number().min(0),\n220:   shadowOnly: z.boolean(),\n221: }).strict();\n222: \n223: const whyRecommendedLaneSchema = laneBreakdownSchema.extend({\n224:   evidenceTypes: z.array(z.string().min(1)),\n225:   evidenceCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n226: }).strict();\n227: \n228: const whyRecommendedSchema = z.object({\n229:   reason: z.string().min(1),\n230:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n231:   topLanes: z.array(whyRecommendedLaneSchema),\n232:   matchedSkillFeatures: z.array(z.object({\n233:     lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n234:     feature: z.string().min(1),\n235:   }).strict()),\n236: }).strict();\n237: \n238: const runtimeLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n239:   liveLaneCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n240:   degradedLanes: z.array(AdvisorLaneSchema),\n241: }).strict();\n242: \n243: const semanticLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n244:   activeEmbedder: z.object({\n245:     name: z.string().min(1),\n246:     dim: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n247:     adapterDim: z.number().int().positive().nullable(),\n248:   }).strict().nullable(),\n249:   vectorCoverage: z.object({\n250:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n251:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n252:     ratio: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n253:   }).strict(),\n254:   dimMismatch: z.boolean(),\n255:   lastRefresh: z.string().nullable(),\n256:   disabledReason: z.string().nullable(),\n257:   laneEnabled: z.boolean(),\n258:   backend: z.object({\n259:     state: z.enum(['reachable', 'unreachable', 'model_missing', 'probe_not_implemented']),\n260:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n261:   }).strict().optional(),\n262:   commandVectorCoverage: z.object({\n263:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n264:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n265:   }).strict().optional(),\n266:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n267: }).strict();\n268: \n269: // NOTE (DEFER decision):\n270: // `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n271: // COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n272: // evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n273: // `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n274: // nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n275: // request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n276: // `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n277: // instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n278: // `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n279: // Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n280: // `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n281: // advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n282: // longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\n283: export const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n284: \n285: export const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n286:   // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n287:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n288:   prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n289:   options: z.object({\n290:     topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n291:     includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n292:     includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n293:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n294:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n295:     includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n296:     // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n297:     // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n298:     compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n299:     // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n300:     // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n301:     surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n302:   }).strict().optional(),\n303: }).strict();\n304: \n305: export const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n306:   skillId: z.string().min(1),\n307:   score: z.number().min(0),\n308:   confidence: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n309:   uncertainty: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n310:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n311:   laneBreakdown: z.array(laneBreakdownSchema).optional(),\n312:   why_recommended: whyRecommendedSchema.optional(),\n313:   matchedDocs: z.array(z.string().min(1)).max(3).optional(),\n314:   redirectFrom: z.array(z.string().min(1)).optional(),\n315:   redirectTo: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n316:   heldBelow: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n317:   status: z.enum(['active', 'deprecated', 'archived', 'future']).optional(),\n318:   workflowMode: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n319:   compiledRoute: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional(),\n320:   // Names the slash command that runs the recommended skill's resolved mode.\n321:   command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n322:   // A command-bearing recommendation also says which face it is (a skill or a\n323:   // command row), how a caller may run it, and which skill owns it. Each stays\n324:   // optional so output from a runtime that predates the fields still parses.\n325:   kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional(),\n326:   policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional(),\n327:   ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n328:   // Set only when a hub held back its command because the prompt names no\n329:   // single mode, so the head can say so.\n330:   needsMode: z.literal(true).optional(),\n331: }).strict();\n332: \n333: export const AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema = z.object({\n334:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n335:   effectiveThresholds: z.object({\n336:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n337:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n338:     confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n339:   }).strict(),\n340:   recommendations: z.array(AdvisorRecommendationSchema),\n341:   ambiguous: z.boolean().optional(),\n342:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n343:   trustState: z.object({\n344:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n345:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n346:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n347:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n348:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n349:   }).strict(),\n350:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n351:   cache: z.object({\n352:     hit: z.boolean(),\n353:     sourceSignaturePresent: z.boolean(),\n354:   }).strict(),\n355:   warnings: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n356:   abstainReasons: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n357:   runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n358:   _shadow: z.object({\n359:     model: z.literal('advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1'),\n360:     liveWeightsFrozen: z.boolean(),\n361:     recommendations: z.array(z.object({\n362:       skillId: z.string().min(1),\n363:       liveScore: z.number().min(0),\n364:       shadowScore: z.number().min(0),\n365:       delta: z.number(),\n366:       dominantShadowLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n367:     }).strict()),\n368:   }).strict().optional(),\n369: }).strict();\n370: \n371: export const AdvisorStatusInputSchema = z.object({\n372:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n373:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema,\n374:   maxMetadataFiles: z.number().int().positive().max(10_000).optional(),\n375:   includeSemanticHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n376:   includeEmbeddingsHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n377:   // Run a read-only SQLite quick_check on the artifact so genuine corruption\n378:   // downgrades freshness to stale (and advisor_rebuild repairs it). Off by\n379:   // default so the read-style advisor_recommend path pays no per-call probe;\n380:   // the advisor_status diagnostic and advisor_rebuild pre-read opt in.\n381:   checkArtifactIntegrity: z.boolean().optional(),\n382:   debug: z.boolean().optional(),\n383: }).strict();\n384: \n385: const embeddingsHealthSchema = z.object({\n386:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n387:   provider: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n388:     z.object({\n389:       state: z.literal('resolved'),\n390:       requestedProvider: z.string(),\n391:       effectiveProvider: z.string(),\n392:       fallbackReason: z.string().nullable(),\n393:       dimensionChanged: z.boolean(),\n394:       reason: z.string(),\n395:     }).strict(),\n396:     z.object({\n397:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n398:       error: z.string().max(200),\n399:     }).strict(),\n400:   ]),\n401:   modelServer: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n402:     z.object({\n403:       state: z.literal('reachable'),\n404:       target: z.string().min(1),\n405:       serverState: z.string().nullable(),\n406:       model: z.string().nullable(),\n407:       dim: z.number().nullable(),\n408:       device: z.string().nullable(),\n409:       loadTimeMs: z.number().nullable(),\n410:       loadStartedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n411:       loadProgressAt: z.string().nullable(),\n412:       lastSuccessfulEmbedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n413:       inFlight: z.number().nullable(),\n414:       queueDepth: z.number().nullable(),\n415:       error: z.string().nullable(),\n416:     }).strict(),\n417:     z.object({\n418:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n419:       target: z.string().min(1),\n420:       errorClass: z.enum(['unreachable', 'timeout', 'bad_response', 'probe_failed']),\n421:       error: z.string(),\n422:     }).strict(),\n423:   ]),\n424: }).strict();\n425: \n426: export const AdvisorStatusOutputSchema = z.object({\n427:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n428:   generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n429:   trustState: z.object({\n430:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n431:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n432:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n433:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n434:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n435:   }).strict(),\n436:   lastGenerationBump: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n437:   lastScanAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n438:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n439:   indexStaleness: z.object({\n440:     state: z.enum(['fresh', 'stale', 'unavailable']),\n441:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n442:     trackedSkills: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n443:     freshSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n444:     changedSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n445:     missingSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n446:     staleSkillIds: z.array(z.string()),\n447:   }).strict().optional(),\n448:   laneWeights: z.record(AdvisorLaneSchema, z.number().min(0)),\n449:   semanticLaneHealth: semanticLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n450:   embeddingsHealth: embeddingsHealthSchema.optional(),\n451:   hookHealth: z.object({\n452:     invocations: z.number().int().positive(),\n453:     rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(),\n454:     rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n455:     rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n456:   }).strict().optional(),\n457:   daemonPid: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n458:   errors: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n459: }).strict();\n460: \n461: export const AdvisorRebuildInputSchema = z.object({\n462:   force: z.boolean().optional(),\n463:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n464:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n465: }).strict();\n466: \n467: export const AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema = z.object({\n468:   rebuilt: z.boolean(),\n469:   skipped: z.boolean(),\n470:   reason: z.enum(['status-live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable', 'force']),\n471:   freshnessBefore: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n472:   freshnessAfter: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n473:   generationBefore: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n474:   generationAfter: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n475:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n476:   summary: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).nullable(),\n477:   diagnostics: z.array(z.string()),\n478: }).strict();\n479: \n480: export const AdvisorValidateInputSchema = z.object({\n481:   confirmHeavyRun: z.literal(true),\n482:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n483:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n484:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable().optional(),\n485:   // Outcome events carry only skill ids + the accept/correct/ignore signal —\n486:   // never the prompt, scenario, or expected skill. This omission is deliberate\n487:   // prompt-safety: telemetry must not store routable prompt content. The\n488:   // consequence is that real misroutes cannot be harvested from telemetry into\n489:   // gold regression cases; gold cases are authored by hand, not reconstructed.\n490:   // Capturing prompts to close that gap would violate the prompt-safety\n491:   // invariant and is intentionally not supported.\n492:   outcomeEvents: z.array(z.object({\n493:     runtime: z.enum(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES),\n494:     outcome: z.enum(['accepted', 'corrected', 'ignored']),\n495:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n496:     correctedSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n497:     timestamp: z.string().datetime().optional(),\n498:   }).strict()).optional(),\n499: }).strict();\n500: \n501: const validationSliceSchema = z.object({\n502:   percentage: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n503:   passed: z.boolean(),\n504:   threshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n505:   count: z.object({\n506:     passed: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n507:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n508:   }).strict(),\n509: }).strict();\n510: \n511: // A named data-slice accuracy gate. Extends the generic validation slice with\n512: // `minN` (the minimum row count below which the slice is statistically\n513: // meaningless and fails, guarding against a corpus edit silently shrinking a\n514: // bucket) and `top1` (the strict top-1 accuracy for the slice, surfaced\n515: // explicitly so operators read the bucket's accuracy without recomputing it\n516: // from `count`).\n517: const bucketSliceSchema = validationSliceSchema.extend({\n518:   minN: z.number().int().positive(),\n519:   top1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n520: }).strict();\n521: \n522: const advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema = z.object({\n523:   fullCorpusTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n524:   holdoutTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n525:   perSkillTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n526:   unknownCountTargetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n527: }).strict().describe('Release-gate thresholds for full corpus, holdout, per-skill accuracy, and UNKNOWN counts.');\n528: \n529: const advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema = z.object({\n530:   confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n531:   uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n532:   confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n533: }).strict().describe('Live runtime routing thresholds surfaced by advisor_validate so manual checks can compare runtime semantics with release gates.');\n534: \n535: const advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema = z.object({\n536:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n537:   recordsRetained: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n538:   rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n539:   rollingP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n540:   rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n541: }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe rolling diagnostics from retained advisor hook telemetry records.');\n542: \n543: const advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema = z.object({\n544:   kind: z.enum(['workspace', 'skill']),\n545:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable(),\n546: }).strict().describe('Whether recorded outcome totals are workspace-wide or scoped to the selected skillSlug.');\n547: \n548: const advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema = z.object({\n549:   accepted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n550:   corrected: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n551:   ignored: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n552: }).strict().describe('Recorded outcome totals retained for the active workspace or skill scope.');\n553: \n554: const advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema = z.object({\n555:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n556:   recordedThisRun: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n557:   scope: advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema,\n558:   totals: advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema,\n559: }).strict().describe('Outcome recording summary, including injected event count and retained accepted/corrected/ignored totals.');\n560: \n561: export const AdvisorValidateOutputSchema = z.object({\n562:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n563:   skillSlug: z.string().nullable(),\n564:   thresholdSemantics: z.object({\n565:     aggregateValidation: advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema,\n566:     runtimeRouting: advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema,\n567:   }).strict().describe('Public threshold contract for advisor_validate, covering release-gate scoring and runtime-routing semantics.'),\n568:   overallAccuracy: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n569:   perSkill: z.array(z.object({\n570:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n571:     status: z.enum(['pass', 'fail', 'skipped']),\n572:     matched: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n573:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n574:   }).strict()),\n575:   slices: z.object({\n576:     corpus: z.object({\n577:       full_corpus_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n578:       unknown_count: z.object({\n579:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n580:         targetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n581:         passed: z.boolean(),\n582:       }).strict(),\n583:       gold_none_false_fire_count: z.object({\n584:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n585:         baselineDelta: z.number().int(),\n586:       }).strict(),\n587:     }).strict(),\n588:     holdout: z.object({\n589:       holdout_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n590:     }).strict(),\n591:     parity: z.object({\n592:       explicit_skill_top1_regression: z.object({\n593:         passed: z.boolean(),\n594:         regressions: z.array(z.string()),\n595:       }).strict(),\n596:       ambiguity_slice_stable: z.object({\n597:         passed: z.boolean(),\n598:         top2Within005: z.boolean(),\n599:       }).strict(),\n600:       derived_lane_attribution_complete: z.boolean(),\n601:     }).strict(),\n602:     safety: z.object({\n603:       adversarial_stuffing_blocked: z.object({\n604:         passed: z.boolean(),\n605:         fixtureCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n606:       }).strict(),\n607:     }).strict(),\n608:     latency: z.object({\n609:       regression_suite_status: z.object({\n610:         p0PassRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n611:         failedCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n612:         commandBridgeFalsePositiveRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n613:         cacheHitP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n614:         uncachedP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n615:       }).strict(),\n616:     }).strict(),\n617:     // Named per-intent accuracy buckets. review/memory_save are corpus rows\n618:     // grouped by their labeled bucket; delegation is the shared executor-routing\n619:     // fixture (the training corpus carries no honest executor-delegation signal).\n620:     // Each is a first-class accuracy gate so a regression confined to one intent\n621:     // class stays visible even when the aggregate corpus number holds.\n622:     buckets: z.object({\n623:       review: bucketSliceSchema,\n624:       memory_save: bucketSliceSchema,\n625:       delegation: bucketSliceSchema,\n626:     }).strict(),\n627:   }).strict(),\n628:   telemetry: z.object({\n629:     diagnostics: advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema,\n630:     outcomes: advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema,\n631:   }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe telemetry diagnostics and recorded outcome summaries exposed for operator validation.'),\n632:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n633: }).strict();\n634: \n635: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n636: // 5. EXPORTS\n637: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n638: \n639: export type AdvisorFreshness = z.infer<typeof AdvisorFreshnessSchema>;\n640: export type AdvisorRecommendInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendInputSchema>;\n641: export type AdvisorRecommendOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema>;\n642: export type AdvisorRebuildInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildInputSchema>;\n643: export type AdvisorRebuildOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema>;\n644: export type AdvisorStatusInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusInputSchema>;\n645: export type AdvisorStatusOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusOutputSchema>;\n646: export type AdvisorValidateInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateInputSchema>;\n647: export type AdvisorValidateOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateOutputSchema>;\n648: \n649: export const AdvisorToolInputSchemas = {\n650:   advisor_recommend: AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n651:   advisor_rebuild: AdvisorRebuildInputSchema,\n652:   advisor_status: AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n653:   advisor_validate: AdvisorValidateInputSchema,\n654: } as const;","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts, lines 1-654\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Tool Schemas\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { z } from 'zod';\n10: import { existsSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES } from '../lib/advisor-runtime-values.js';\n14: import { SCORER_LANE_IDS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n15: \n16: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17: // 2. CONSTANTS\n18: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: \n20: export const AdvisorFreshnessSchema = z.enum(['live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable']);\n21: export const AdvisorLaneSchema = z.enum(SCORER_LANE_IDS);\n22: \n23: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: // 3. HELPERS\n25: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n26: \n27: // Bound caller-supplied workspaceRoot inputs to a small\n28: // allowlist (repo root + os.tmpdir()) so handlers cannot be coerced into\n29: // resolving paths outside the workspace. resolve() canonicalizes the input\n30: // path; realpathSync follows symlinks; the prefix check rejects anything\n31: // that escapes the allowlist after canonicalization.\n32: //\n33: // Directory names the source tree may sit under. A checkout may link one to the\n34: // other, so both mark the same tree.\n35: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n36: \n37: // Repo root is detected by walking up from process.cwd() looking for the\n38: // system-spec-kit SKILL.md sentinel — same shape as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot but\n39: // inlined here to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/. The start\n40: // directory is a parameter so the lockstep test can feed both resolvers one tree.\n41: export function detectRepoRoot(start: string = process.cwd()): string {\n42:   // Use the same SKILL.md file sentinel as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot so the schema\n43:   // and the handler agree on which directory is the workspace root. A bare\n44:   // directory sentinel would match the nested mock trees other workflows create.\n45:   // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, so the sentinel is\n46:   // tested under both.\n47:   const sentinels = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => `${name}/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`);\n48:   let current = resolve(start);\n49:   for (let index = 0; index < 14; index += 1) {\n50:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n51:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n52:     if (parent === current) break;\n53:     current = parent;\n54:   }\n55:   // Lockstep with findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot: when the walk misses the sentinel,\n56:   // never anchor the allowlist on a directory inside a source tree. Take the start\n57:   // or the nearest source-root parent that holds the sentinel, else hoist above the\n58:   // outermost source-root segment, so caller-supplied workspaceRoots are bounded\n59:   // to the real root, not a nested subdir.\n60:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n61: }\n62: \n63: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:nearestSentinelHolder, kept local for\n64: // the same reason as the hoist below. A capped walk misses the sentinel, yet the root\n65: // is still the start or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path, so\n66: // testing the start and then those parents nearest first keeps a repository that\n67: // sits under a directory named .skilled or .opencode.\n68: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n69:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n70:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n71:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n72:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n73:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n74:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n75:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n76:   }\n77:   return null;\n78: }\n79: \n80: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:hoistAboveOpencodeTree. Kept local\n81: // to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/ — the two must stay in\n82: // lockstep so the schema allowlist and the handler agree on the workspace root.\n83: // A `.skilled` or `.opencode` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n84: // root, so hoisting above the OUTERMOST one yields the real root and can never\n85: // return a path inside a source tree (the earlier specs-only shape missed sibling\n86: // subtrees like skills/).\n87: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n88:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n89:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n90:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n91:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n92:     }\n93:   }\n94:   return null;\n95: }\n96: \n97: function canonicalize(input: string): string {\n98:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n99:   try {\n100:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n101:   } catch {\n102:     // Path may not exist yet (test fixtures created lazily,\n103:     // tmpdir mkdtemp paths probed before mkdir). Walk up and realpath the\n104:     // first existing ancestor, then re-join the unresolved tail. This\n105:     // resolves macOS-style symlinks like /tmp → /private/tmp even when\n106:     // the leaf doesn't exist.\n107:     let probe = resolved;\n108:     let tail = '';\n109:     for (let depth = 0; depth < 32; depth += 1) {\n110:       const parent = resolve(probe, '..');\n111:       if (parent === probe) break;\n112:       try {\n113:         const realParent = realpathSync.native(parent);\n114:         return tail\n115:           ? resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1) + tail)\n116:           : resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1));\n117:       } catch {\n118:         // Parent doesn't exist either — keep walking up.\n119:         const segment = probe.slice(parent.length + 1);\n120:         tail = tail ? `${segment}/${tail}` : segment;\n121:         probe = parent;\n122:       }\n123:     }\n124:     return resolved;\n125:   }\n126: }\n127: \n128: const SOURCE_REPO_ROOT = canonicalize(detectRepoRoot());\n129: \n130: const ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES: readonly string[] = (() => {\n131:   const prefixes: string[] = [];\n132:   prefixes.push(SOURCE_REPO_ROOT);\n133:   prefixes.push(canonicalize(tmpdir()));\n134:   // Include the canonicalized /tmp prefix as well. On macOS\n135:   // os.tmpdir() returns the per-user temp dir under /var/folders/...; the\n136:   // /tmp symlink resolves to /private/tmp. Test fixtures and tools that\n137:   // hardcode /tmp/foo paths need both forms in the allowlist.\n138:   prefixes.push(canonicalize('/tmp'));\n139:   // Accept additional explicit allowlist via env (CI / test runners).\n140:   const envExtras = process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST;\n141:   if (envExtras) {\n142:     for (const extra of envExtras.split(':')) {\n143:       const trimmed = extra.trim();\n144:       if (trimmed) prefixes.push(canonicalize(trimmed));\n145:     }\n146:   }\n147:   return Array.from(new Set(prefixes));\n148: })();\n149: \n150: /**\n151:  * Validate that a caller-supplied workspaceRoot resolves under\n152:  * the repo root, os.tmpdir(), or an explicit allowlist entry after\n153:  * realpath canonicalization.\n154:  *\n155:  * Exported so handlers can re-canonicalize at call time and reuse the\n156:  * same bounding logic the schema applies at parse time.\n157:  */\n158: export function isAllowedWorkspaceRoot(input: string): boolean {\n159:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n160:   const canonical = canonicalize(input);\n161:   return ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES.some(\n162:     (prefix) => canonical === prefix || canonical.startsWith(`${prefix}/`),\n163:   ) || isWiredToSourceTree(canonical);\n164: }\n165: \n166: function realpathOrNull(path: string): string | null {\n167:   try {\n168:     return realpathSync.native(path);\n169:   } catch {\n170:     return null;\n171:   }\n172: }\n173: \n174: /**\n175:  * True when the input, or a directory above it, holds a source-root entry\n176:  * (`.skilled` or `.opencode`) whose realpath is the source tree's own entry.\n177:  *\n178:  * A project linked to a shared checkout holds `.skilled -> <source>/.skilled`\n179:  * while the daemon runs from the source tree, so the prefix allowlist alone\n180:  * refuses every linked project. Matching realpaths admits only a workspace that\n181:  * is actually wired to this source; a copied tree or a link to another source\n182:  * resolves elsewhere and stays refused.\n183:  */\n184: export function isWiredToSourceTree(input: string, sourceRoot: string = SOURCE_REPO_ROOT): boolean {\n185:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n186:   const sourceEntries = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES\n187:     .map((name) => realpathOrNull(resolve(sourceRoot, name)))\n188:     .filter((entry): entry is string => entry !== null);\n189:   if (sourceEntries.length === 0) return false;\n190:   let current = canonicalize(input);\n191:   for (let depth = 0; depth < 64; depth += 1) {\n192:     for (const name of SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES) {\n193:       const entry = realpathOrNull(resolve(current, name));\n194:       if (entry !== null && sourceEntries.includes(entry)) return true;\n195:     }\n196:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n197:     if (parent === current) break;\n198:     current = parent;\n199:   }\n200:   return false;\n201: }\n202: \n203: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n204: // 4. SCHEMA DEFINITIONS\n205: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n206: \n207: const BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema = z\n208:   .string()\n209:   .min(1)\n210:   .refine(isAllowedWorkspaceRoot, {\n211:     message:\n212:       'workspaceRoot must resolve under the repo root, os.tmpdir(), an explicit SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST entry, or a project whose .skilled links to this source tree',\n213:   });\n214: \n215: const laneBreakdownSchema = z.object({\n216:   lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n217:   rawScore: z.number().min(0),\n218:   weightedScore: z.number().min(0),\n219:   weight: z.number().min(0),\n220:   shadowOnly: z.boolean(),\n221: }).strict();\n222: \n223: const whyRecommendedLaneSchema = laneBreakdownSchema.extend({\n224:   evidenceTypes: z.array(z.string().min(1)),\n225:   evidenceCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n226: }).strict();\n227: \n228: const whyRecommendedSchema = z.object({\n229:   reason: z.string().min(1),\n230:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n231:   topLanes: z.array(whyRecommendedLaneSchema),\n232:   matchedSkillFeatures: z.array(z.object({\n233:     lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n234:     feature: z.string().min(1),\n235:   }).strict()),\n236: }).strict();\n237: \n238: const runtimeLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n239:   liveLaneCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n240:   degradedLanes: z.array(AdvisorLaneSchema),\n241: }).strict();\n242: \n243: const semanticLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n244:   activeEmbedder: z.object({\n245:     name: z.string().min(1),\n246:     dim: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n247:     adapterDim: z.number().int().positive().nullable(),\n248:   }).strict().nullable(),\n249:   vectorCoverage: z.object({\n250:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n251:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n252:     ratio: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n253:   }).strict(),\n254:   dimMismatch: z.boolean(),\n255:   lastRefresh: z.string().nullable(),\n256:   disabledReason: z.string().nullable(),\n257:   laneEnabled: z.boolean(),\n258:   backend: z.object({\n259:     state: z.enum(['reachable', 'unreachable', 'model_missing', 'probe_not_implemented']),\n260:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n261:   }).strict().optional(),\n262:   commandVectorCoverage: z.object({\n263:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n264:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n265:   }).strict().optional(),\n266:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n267: }).strict();\n268: \n269: // NOTE (DEFER decision):\n270: // `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n271: // COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n272: // evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n273: // `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n274: // nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n275: // request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n276: // `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n277: // instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n278: // `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n279: // Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n280: // `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n281: // advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n282: // longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\n283: export const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n284: \n285: export const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n286:   // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n287:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n288:   prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n289:   options: z.object({\n290:     topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n291:     includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n292:     includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n293:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n294:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n295:     includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n296:     // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n297:     // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n298:     compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n299:     // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n300:     // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n301:     surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n302:   }).strict().optional(),\n303: }).strict();\n304: \n305: export const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n306:   skillId: z.string().min(1),\n307:   score: z.number().min(0),\n308:   confidence: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n309:   uncertainty: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n310:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n311:   laneBreakdown: z.array(laneBreakdownSchema).optional(),\n312:   why_recommended: whyRecommendedSchema.optional(),\n313:   matchedDocs: z.array(z.string().min(1)).max(3).optional(),\n314:   redirectFrom: z.array(z.string().min(1)).optional(),\n315:   redirectTo: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n316:   heldBelow: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n317:   status: z.enum(['active', 'deprecated', 'archived', 'future']).optional(),\n318:   workflowMode: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n319:   compiledRoute: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional(),\n320:   // Names the slash command that runs the recommended skill's resolved mode.\n321:   command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n322:   // A command-bearing recommendation also says which face it is (a skill or a\n323:   // command row), how a caller may run it, and which skill owns it. Each stays\n324:   // optional so output from a runtime that predates the fields still parses.\n325:   kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional(),\n326:   policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional(),\n327:   ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n328:   // Set only when a hub held back its command because the prompt names no\n329:   // single mode, so the head can say so.\n330:   needsMode: z.literal(true).optional(),\n331: }).strict();\n332: \n333: export const AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema = z.object({\n334:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n335:   effectiveThresholds: z.object({\n336:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n337:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n338:     confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n339:   }).strict(),\n340:   recommendations: z.array(AdvisorRecommendationSchema),\n341:   ambiguous: z.boolean().optional(),\n342:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n343:   trustState: z.object({\n344:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n345:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n346:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n347:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n348:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n349:   }).strict(),\n350:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n351:   cache: z.object({\n352:     hit: z.boolean(),\n353:     sourceSignaturePresent: z.boolean(),\n354:   }).strict(),\n355:   warnings: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n356:   abstainReasons: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n357:   runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n358:   _shadow: z.object({\n359:     model: z.literal('advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1'),\n360:     liveWeightsFrozen: z.boolean(),\n361:     recommendations: z.array(z.object({\n362:       skillId: z.string().min(1),\n363:       liveScore: z.number().min(0),\n364:       shadowScore: z.number().min(0),\n365:       delta: z.number(),\n366:       dominantShadowLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n367:     }).strict()),\n368:   }).strict().optional(),\n369: }).strict();\n370: \n371: export const AdvisorStatusInputSchema = z.object({\n372:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n373:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema,\n374:   maxMetadataFiles: z.number().int().positive().max(10_000).optional(),\n375:   includeSemanticHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n376:   includeEmbeddingsHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n377:   // Run a read-only SQLite quick_check on the artifact so genuine corruption\n378:   // downgrades freshness to stale (and advisor_rebuild repairs it). Off by\n379:   // default so the read-style advisor_recommend path pays no per-call probe;\n380:   // the advisor_status diagnostic and advisor_rebuild pre-read opt in.\n381:   checkArtifactIntegrity: z.boolean().optional(),\n382:   debug: z.boolean().optional(),\n383: }).strict();\n384: \n385: const embeddingsHealthSchema = z.object({\n386:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n387:   provider: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n388:     z.object({\n389:       state: z.literal('resolved'),\n390:       requestedProvider: z.string(),\n391:       effectiveProvider: z.string(),\n392:       fallbackReason: z.string().nullable(),\n393:       dimensionChanged: z.boolean(),\n394:       reason: z.string(),\n395:     }).strict(),\n396:     z.object({\n397:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n398:       error: z.string().max(200),\n399:     }).strict(),\n400:   ]),\n401:   modelServer: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n402:     z.object({\n403:       state: z.literal('reachable'),\n404:       target: z.string().min(1),\n405:       serverState: z.string().nullable(),\n406:       model: z.string().nullable(),\n407:       dim: z.number().nullable(),\n408:       device: z.string().nullable(),\n409:       loadTimeMs: z.number().nullable(),\n410:       loadStartedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n411:       loadProgressAt: z.string().nullable(),\n412:       lastSuccessfulEmbedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n413:       inFlight: z.number().nullable(),\n414:       queueDepth: z.number().nullable(),\n415:       error: z.string().nullable(),\n416:     }).strict(),\n417:     z.object({\n418:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n419:       target: z.string().min(1),\n420:       errorClass: z.enum(['unreachable', 'timeout', 'bad_response', 'probe_failed']),\n421:       error: z.string(),\n422:     }).strict(),\n423:   ]),\n424: }).strict();\n425: \n426: export const AdvisorStatusOutputSchema = z.object({\n427:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n428:   generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n429:   trustState: z.object({\n430:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n431:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n432:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n433:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n434:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n435:   }).strict(),\n436:   lastGenerationBump: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n437:   lastScanAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n438:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n439:   indexStaleness: z.object({\n440:     state: z.enum(['fresh', 'stale', 'unavailable']),\n441:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n442:     trackedSkills: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n443:     freshSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n444:     changedSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n445:     missingSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n446:     staleSkillIds: z.array(z.string()),\n447:   }).strict().optional(),\n448:   laneWeights: z.record(AdvisorLaneSchema, z.number().min(0)),\n449:   semanticLaneHealth: semanticLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n450:   embeddingsHealth: embeddingsHealthSchema.optional(),\n451:   hookHealth: z.object({\n452:     invocations: z.number().int().positive(),\n453:     rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(),\n454:     rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n455:     rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n456:   }).strict().optional(),\n457:   daemonPid: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n458:   errors: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n459: }).strict();\n460: \n461: export const AdvisorRebuildInputSchema = z.object({\n462:   force: z.boolean().optional(),\n463:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n464:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n465: }).strict();\n466: \n467: export const AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema = z.object({\n468:   rebuilt: z.boolean(),\n469:   skipped: z.boolean(),\n470:   reason: z.enum(['status-live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable', 'force']),\n471:   freshnessBefore: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n472:   freshnessAfter: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n473:   generationBefore: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n474:   generationAfter: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n475:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n476:   summary: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).nullable(),\n477:   diagnostics: z.array(z.string()),\n478: }).strict();\n479: \n480: export const AdvisorValidateInputSchema = z.object({\n481:   confirmHeavyRun: z.literal(true),\n482:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n483:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n484:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable().optional(),\n485:   // Outcome events carry only skill ids + the accept/correct/ignore signal —\n486:   // never the prompt, scenario, or expected skill. This omission is deliberate\n487:   // prompt-safety: telemetry must not store routable prompt content. The\n488:   // consequence is that real misroutes cannot be harvested from telemetry into\n489:   // gold regression cases; gold cases are authored by hand, not reconstructed.\n490:   // Capturing prompts to close that gap would violate the prompt-safety\n491:   // invariant and is intentionally not supported.\n492:   outcomeEvents: z.array(z.object({\n493:     runtime: z.enum(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES),\n494:     outcome: z.enum(['accepted', 'corrected', 'ignored']),\n495:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n496:     correctedSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n497:     timestamp: z.string().datetime().optional(),\n498:   }).strict()).optional(),\n499: }).strict();\n500: \n501: const validationSliceSchema = z.object({\n502:   percentage: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n503:   passed: z.boolean(),\n504:   threshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n505:   count: z.object({\n506:     passed: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n507:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n508:   }).strict(),\n509: }).strict();\n510: \n511: // A named data-slice accuracy gate. Extends the generic validation slice with\n512: // `minN` (the minimum row count below which the slice is statistically\n513: // meaningless and fails, guarding against a corpus edit silently shrinking a\n514: // bucket) and `top1` (the strict top-1 accuracy for the slice, surfaced\n515: // explicitly so operators read the bucket's accuracy without recomputing it\n516: // from `count`).\n517: const bucketSliceSchema = validationSliceSchema.extend({\n518:   minN: z.number().int().positive(),\n519:   top1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n520: }).strict();\n521: \n522: const advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema = z.object({\n523:   fullCorpusTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n524:   holdoutTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n525:   perSkillTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n526:   unknownCountTargetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n527: }).strict().describe('Release-gate thresholds for full corpus, holdout, per-skill accuracy, and UNKNOWN counts.');\n528: \n529: const advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema = z.object({\n530:   confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n531:   uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n532:   confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n533: }).strict().describe('Live runtime routing thresholds surfaced by advisor_validate so manual checks can compare runtime semantics with release gates.');\n534: \n535: const advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema = z.object({\n536:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n537:   recordsRetained: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n538:   rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n539:   rollingP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n540:   rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n541: }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe rolling diagnostics from retained advisor hook telemetry records.');\n542: \n543: const advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema = z.object({\n544:   kind: z.enum(['workspace', 'skill']),\n545:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable(),\n546: }).strict().describe('Whether recorded outcome totals are workspace-wide or scoped to the selected skillSlug.');\n547: \n548: const advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema = z.object({\n549:   accepted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n550:   corrected: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n551:   ignored: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n552: }).strict().describe('Recorded outcome totals retained for the active workspace or skill scope.');\n553: \n554: const advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema = z.object({\n555:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n556:   recordedThisRun: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n557:   scope: advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema,\n558:   totals: advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema,\n559: }).strict().describe('Outcome recording summary, including injected event count and retained accepted/corrected/ignored totals.');\n560: \n561: export const AdvisorValidateOutputSchema = z.object({\n562:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n563:   skillSlug: z.string().nullable(),\n564:   thresholdSemantics: z.object({\n565:     aggregateValidation: advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema,\n566:     runtimeRouting: advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema,\n567:   }).strict().describe('Public threshold contract for advisor_validate, covering release-gate scoring and runtime-routing semantics.'),\n568:   overallAccuracy: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n569:   perSkill: z.array(z.object({\n570:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n571:     status: z.enum(['pass', 'fail', 'skipped']),\n572:     matched: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n573:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n574:   }).strict()),\n575:   slices: z.object({\n576:     corpus: z.object({\n577:       full_corpus_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n578:       unknown_count: z.object({\n579:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n580:         targetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n581:         passed: z.boolean(),\n582:       }).strict(),\n583:       gold_none_false_fire_count: z.object({\n584:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n585:         baselineDelta: z.number().int(),\n586:       }).strict(),\n587:     }).strict(),\n588:     holdout: z.object({\n589:       holdout_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n590:     }).strict(),\n591:     parity: z.object({\n592:       explicit_skill_top1_regression: z.object({\n593:         passed: z.boolean(),\n594:         regressions: z.array(z.string()),\n595:       }).strict(),\n596:       ambiguity_slice_stable: z.object({\n597:         passed: z.boolean(),\n598:         top2Within005: z.boolean(),\n599:       }).strict(),\n600:       derived_lane_attribution_complete: z.boolean(),\n601:     }).strict(),\n602:     safety: z.object({\n603:       adversarial_stuffing_blocked: z.object({\n604:         passed: z.boolean(),\n605:         fixtureCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n606:       }).strict(),\n607:     }).strict(),\n608:     latency: z.object({\n609:       regression_suite_status: z.object({\n610:         p0PassRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n611:         failedCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n612:         commandBridgeFalsePositiveRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n613:         cacheHitP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n614:         uncachedP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n615:       }).strict(),\n616:     }).strict(),\n617:     // Named per-intent accuracy buckets. review/memory_save are corpus rows\n618:     // grouped by their labeled bucket; delegation is the shared executor-routing\n619:     // fixture (the training corpus carries no honest executor-delegation signal).\n620:     // Each is a first-class accuracy gate so a regression confined to one intent\n621:     // class stays visible even when the aggregate corpus number holds.\n622:     buckets: z.object({\n623:       review: bucketSliceSchema,\n624:       memory_save: bucketSliceSchema,\n625:       delegation: bucketSliceSchema,\n626:     }).strict(),\n627:   }).strict(),\n628:   telemetry: z.object({\n629:     diagnostics: advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema,\n630:     outcomes: advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema,\n631:   }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe telemetry diagnostics and recorded outcome summaries exposed for operator validation.'),\n632:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n633: }).strict();\n634: \n635: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n636: // 5. EXPORTS\n637: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n638: \n639: export type AdvisorFreshness = z.infer<typeof AdvisorFreshnessSchema>;\n640: export type AdvisorRecommendInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendInputSchema>;\n641: export type AdvisorRecommendOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema>;\n642: export type AdvisorRebuildInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildInputSchema>;\n643: export type AdvisorRebuildOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema>;\n644: export type AdvisorStatusInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusInputSchema>;\n645: export type AdvisorStatusOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusOutputSchema>;\n646: export type AdvisorValidateInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateInputSchema>;\n647: export type AdvisorValidateOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateOutputSchema>;\n648: \n649: export const AdvisorToolInputSchemas = {\n650:   advisor_recommend: AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n651:   advisor_rebuild: AdvisorRebuildInputSchema,\n652:   advisor_status: AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n653:   advisor_validate: AdvisorValidateInputSchema,\n654: } as const;"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794565099569,"end":1794565100007}}}}
